1
00:00:33,459 --> 00:00:35,819
Chuck, see what it is.

2
00:00:41,284 --> 00:00:43,203
Hey, Miller,
we got something.

3
00:00:43,348 --> 00:00:46,576
- Well, what is it?
- Will you just come here?

4
00:00:49,793 --> 00:00:51,093
Well, I'll be.

5
00:00:51,157 --> 00:00:52,490
They were right.

6
00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:54,879
Yeah, I thought
it was a bunch of bull.

7
00:00:55,241 --> 00:00:57,391
Who was right?
What are you guys talking about?

8
00:00:57,416 --> 00:00:58,535
Where've you been for the last month, kid?

9
00:00:58,560 --> 00:01:00,133
Why do think the Indians
have been picketing there...

10
00:01:00,158 --> 00:01:01,475
ever since we started this job?

11
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,801
Yeah, man. They're claiming we're
disturbing some ancient burial ground.

12
00:01:04,921 --> 00:01:07,314
But the Katona tribe is
more than 20 miles away.

13
00:01:07,362 --> 00:01:08,420
Yeah, I know.

14
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:12,071
But they think anytime someone finds
a freaking arrowhead around here,

15
00:01:12,107 --> 00:01:14,618
the land is theirs
and they want it back.

16
00:01:14,713 --> 00:01:15,939
Man.

17
00:01:16,391 --> 00:01:18,559
This thing looks over 100 years old.

18
00:01:18,638 --> 00:01:21,281
Yeah. It's gonna look good in my den
under that moose head.

19
00:01:21,306 --> 00:01:23,706
Hey, man, wait, wait, wait!

20
00:01:26,234 --> 00:01:27,259
What was that?

21
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:28,322
Nothing.

22
00:01:28,347 --> 00:01:29,394
Come on, guys.

23
00:01:29,419 --> 00:01:31,728
We got to clear out this junk,
so we can finish the job.

24
00:01:31,753 --> 00:01:34,263
Now hit it with that pickax
and try to break it up.

25
00:01:34,297 --> 00:01:35,636
Break it up?

26
00:01:35,661 --> 00:01:38,156
Shouldn't we try to save it?
It might be worth something.

27
00:01:38,578 --> 00:01:41,021
What do you say, son?
Give me that pick.

28
00:01:46,716 --> 00:01:48,671
What the hell was that?

29
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:51,740
You think those picketers
are out there beyond the lights?

30
00:01:51,889 --> 00:01:55,328
Yeah. They're probably getting
a good laugh at our expense too.

31
00:01:57,276 --> 00:01:59,587
Jeez, that guy is a hothead.

32
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,243
Well, let's just see 'em
come any closer.

33
00:02:06,306 --> 00:02:08,289
Miller, you're taking this
way too far, man.

34
00:02:08,314 --> 00:02:09,489
Give me that.

35
00:02:09,521 --> 00:02:11,556
Come on, guys.
Let's, let's get out of here.

36
00:02:11,603 --> 00:02:13,218
Not till we finish.

37
00:02:13,282 --> 00:02:15,131
Riley, help me.

38
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:26,889
What the hell was that?
An earthquake?

39
00:02:29,124 --> 00:02:30,830
I don't know.

40
00:02:31,104 --> 00:02:32,943
I think Hanson's right.

41
00:02:33,001 --> 00:02:34,817
I say, we call it a night, fellas.

42
00:02:34,849 --> 00:02:37,066
Riley, I've changed my mind.

43
00:02:37,368 --> 00:02:39,844
That sounds like a good idea.

44
00:03:48,996 --> 00:03:50,887
Come get it.

45
00:06:08,805 --> 00:06:10,206
Hey.

46
00:06:14,695 --> 00:06:16,594
- Hi, honey.
- Hi, Dad.

47
00:06:16,619 --> 00:06:18,166
Oh-oh-oh.

48
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,600
Look at you.

49
00:06:22,176 --> 00:06:24,346
You have grown up.

50
00:06:24,695 --> 00:06:26,925
That's what happens.

51
00:06:27,192 --> 00:06:29,444
Yeah, I guess so.

52
00:06:29,626 --> 00:06:32,812
Guess it's just more dramatic
'cause you're not here all the time.

53
00:06:36,381 --> 00:06:38,405
Well, uh, here, let me take this.

54
00:06:38,430 --> 00:06:40,810
Uh, let's get moving, huh?

55
00:06:46,674 --> 00:06:49,453
Your mother have
any instructions for me?

56
00:06:50,048 --> 00:06:51,340
Instructions?

57
00:06:51,365 --> 00:06:53,031
Yeah, like the last time
you came out,

58
00:06:53,056 --> 00:06:55,034
she told me how to wash your clothes.

59
00:06:55,105 --> 00:06:57,641
Even told me how to make your toast.

60
00:06:57,689 --> 00:06:59,207
That was two years ago.

61
00:06:59,248 --> 00:07:01,478
I can make my own toast now.

62
00:07:01,860 --> 00:07:03,114
Wow!

63
00:07:03,139 --> 00:07:04,883
You have grown up.

64
00:07:04,908 --> 00:07:06,884
You said that already.

65
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:13,166
Look, your mother's in Europe
for the summer, so...

66
00:07:13,395 --> 00:07:16,047
like it or not,
we are stuck with each other.

67
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:19,979
You know, we can make it go
a whole lot quicker if we're at least...

68
00:07:20,181 --> 00:07:22,295
civil with each other.

69
00:07:22,335 --> 00:07:23,962
Hm?

70
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:29,198
I don't suppose she gave you
any instructions on how to do that.

71
00:07:29,508 --> 00:07:30,869
No.

72
00:07:31,755 --> 00:07:34,185
I guess we're on our own.

73
00:07:48,688 --> 00:07:50,642
What's all that?

74
00:07:51,909 --> 00:07:54,617
Oh, a developer is building
a swanky resort.

75
00:07:54,642 --> 00:07:56,742
Katonas are all up in arms about it.

76
00:07:56,775 --> 00:07:58,562
A swanky resort?

77
00:07:58,613 --> 00:08:00,126
Here?

78
00:08:00,342 --> 00:08:01,548
I know.

79
00:08:01,573 --> 00:08:02,902
Come on, I'll get your bag.

80
00:08:02,927 --> 00:08:05,009
It's okay. I got it.

81
00:08:06,125 --> 00:08:08,378
Just like your mother.

82
00:08:20,862 --> 00:08:22,782
Dex, I told you before.
Don't call me here.

83
00:08:22,807 --> 00:08:23,981
I'll see you tonight.

84
00:08:24,006 --> 00:08:25,123
Morning, Sheriff.

85
00:08:25,148 --> 00:08:26,278
Lolli, what's new?

86
00:08:26,303 --> 00:08:28,548
Besides you having a date
with Dex tonight?

87
00:08:28,595 --> 00:08:31,313
Did the picketers
give you any trouble?

88
00:08:31,408 --> 00:08:33,109
No, I just walked by.

89
00:08:33,134 --> 00:08:34,803
Where's Kelly?

90
00:08:34,986 --> 00:08:36,914
She's coming in.

91
00:08:37,081 --> 00:08:38,972
Even when you're together,
you're not together.

92
00:08:38,997 --> 00:08:41,212
Lolli, is anything happening?

93
00:08:41,285 --> 00:08:43,018
Well, Sadie Riley called,

94
00:08:43,043 --> 00:08:45,264
said, Paul didn't
make it home last night.

95
00:08:45,542 --> 00:08:48,019
Maybe, he's just pulled another
all-nighter out at the site.

96
00:08:48,044 --> 00:08:51,312
- I mean, they're working 'em like hell.
- Yeah, Dex told me that.

97
00:08:51,535 --> 00:08:53,428
I don't think so, Sheriff.

98
00:08:53,468 --> 00:08:54,547
That was Lisa Miller.

99
00:08:54,572 --> 00:08:57,617
Neil was supposed to take their kid
to school this morning, never came home.

100
00:08:57,642 --> 00:09:00,186
He was working out at
the Krantz site too, wasn't he?

101
00:09:00,265 --> 00:09:01,924
I think so.

102
00:09:03,825 --> 00:09:05,405
Hey, Mark, take the second car.

103
00:09:05,430 --> 00:09:08,230
Go out along 81.
I'll check the 395.

104
00:09:08,268 --> 00:09:09,506
Maybe, they got in a wreck.

105
00:09:09,537 --> 00:09:10,645
On my way.

106
00:09:10,670 --> 00:09:12,114
And I'll meet you out at the site.

107
00:09:12,154 --> 00:09:13,701
Copy that.

108
00:09:16,345 --> 00:09:18,796
Big Jim, what are you doing here?

109
00:09:18,905 --> 00:09:21,506
In case you haven't noticed,
the sun is up.

110
00:09:22,017 --> 00:09:24,334
Well, truth be told,

111
00:09:24,877 --> 00:09:27,123
today I got babysitting duties.

112
00:09:27,148 --> 00:09:28,488
What are you talking about?

113
00:09:28,513 --> 00:09:30,993
Well, the, the field trip,
the university kids,

114
00:09:31,018 --> 00:09:33,129
the, the archeology class.
Remember that?

115
00:09:33,154 --> 00:09:34,768
Oh, right, right, right.
When is that?

116
00:09:34,793 --> 00:09:36,756
I'm on my way over there right now.

117
00:09:36,796 --> 00:09:39,574
Well, keep an eye out for Miller's truck
while you're out there, okay?

118
00:09:39,599 --> 00:09:40,732
Yeah, sure. See you later.

119
00:09:40,757 --> 00:09:42,058
Yeah.

120
00:09:46,489 --> 00:09:48,190
- Kel!
- Hey!

121
00:09:48,215 --> 00:09:49,928
My Kelly belly.

122
00:09:51,304 --> 00:09:52,495
Oh, girl.

123
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:53,741
Look at you.

124
00:09:53,767 --> 00:09:55,392
Hollywood is working for you.

125
00:09:55,417 --> 00:09:57,447
You look just one
of those Hollywood hotties.

126
00:09:57,472 --> 00:10:00,125
I don't even live in LA, Loll.
I live in Upland.

127
00:10:00,150 --> 00:10:02,379
Well, it's still 1,000 miles
closer than I'll ever get.

128
00:10:02,404 --> 00:10:05,102
Well, don't go too far.
I need you to hold the fort.

129
00:10:05,316 --> 00:10:06,484
Listen, Kel, uh...

130
00:10:06,509 --> 00:10:08,666
I gotta make a run.
I'll be back in an hour or so.

131
00:10:08,722 --> 00:10:11,008
Then, we'll get you situated, okay?

132
00:10:11,349 --> 00:10:12,557
I got it covered.

133
00:10:12,582 --> 00:10:13,850
All right.

134
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:36,603
Pomeroy, it's 8:20.
Where are the cement trucks?

135
00:10:36,647 --> 00:10:37,992
Why aren't we pouring?

136
00:10:38,017 --> 00:10:39,733
The foundations aren't ready yet, sir.

137
00:10:39,758 --> 00:10:41,354
I thought you had that handled.

138
00:10:41,379 --> 00:10:44,317
- Well, I, I did, sir, but--
- But what?

139
00:10:44,987 --> 00:10:47,678
You told me you had
your best men on this all night.

140
00:10:47,940 --> 00:10:49,007
I did.

141
00:10:49,032 --> 00:10:51,072
Well, where are they?
Why isn't the job done?

142
00:10:51,104 --> 00:10:52,744
Well, that's just the thing, Mr. Krantz.

143
00:10:52,769 --> 00:10:54,894
When Dex and I showed up
this morning, they were gone.

144
00:10:54,919 --> 00:10:56,410
- They quit?
- Jimmy!

145
00:10:56,524 --> 00:10:58,539
I don't think so.
Their cars are still here. And--

146
00:10:58,564 --> 00:11:00,159
And what?

147
00:11:00,661 --> 00:11:01,886
Dad!

148
00:11:01,949 --> 00:11:03,457
- Dad!
- Not now, Dex.

149
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:04,711
We found more.

150
00:11:04,743 --> 00:11:05,902
Lots more.

151
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:08,234
What are you talking about?
You found what?

152
00:11:08,967 --> 00:11:11,053
I think you should see this
for yourself, Mr. Krantz.

153
00:11:11,078 --> 00:11:12,451
This way, please.

154
00:11:12,476 --> 00:11:14,382
Jimmy, wait here.

155
00:11:37,148 --> 00:11:39,332
This is all I need.

156
00:11:42,084 --> 00:11:44,666
This could be an incredible find,
Mr. Krantz.

157
00:11:44,714 --> 00:11:46,405
Right.

158
00:11:46,632 --> 00:11:48,307
Cover it up.

159
00:11:48,878 --> 00:11:50,347
- What?
- Not now, Dex.

160
00:11:50,372 --> 00:11:52,030
You heard me.

161
00:11:52,078 --> 00:11:55,320
Pomeroy, I told you
I want it buried.

162
00:11:55,941 --> 00:11:57,321
But, Mr. Krantz,
Dex has a point.

163
00:11:57,346 --> 00:11:59,474
- This is--
- No "buts," Pomeroy.

164
00:11:59,762 --> 00:12:02,059
The Native American Council
finds about this,

165
00:12:02,084 --> 00:12:04,459
they could shut me down
for weeks, possibly years.

166
00:12:04,484 --> 00:12:06,419
I've got too much invested in this...

167
00:12:06,451 --> 00:12:08,975
to see shoot it down
the tubes right now.

168
00:12:09,204 --> 00:12:11,161
Understood.

169
00:12:11,560 --> 00:12:13,371
Dex, you know what to do.

170
00:12:13,414 --> 00:12:15,595
Get the survey team started
on the second quadrant.

171
00:12:15,639 --> 00:12:17,486
And you tell 'em...

172
00:12:17,669 --> 00:12:20,654
if they find any more of these relics,

173
00:12:20,848 --> 00:12:24,145
I want 'em bagged and
sent straight back to me.

174
00:12:24,843 --> 00:12:27,431
Son, you heard the man.
Get going.

175
00:12:28,153 --> 00:12:30,338
Whatever you say, Dad.

176
00:12:34,259 --> 00:12:35,673
All right.

177
00:12:35,872 --> 00:12:39,346
How many men beside you
and your boy know about this?

178
00:12:40,314 --> 00:12:41,854
Just the morning crew of 10, sir.

179
00:12:41,909 --> 00:12:43,627
Tell them, I'm gonna
double their salary,

180
00:12:43,652 --> 00:12:46,572
and I want them on the Hawaiian
project as of tomorrow.

181
00:12:46,695 --> 00:12:48,798
Jimmy'll make all the arrangements.

182
00:12:48,869 --> 00:12:51,435
What about Miller and
the other two that split last night?

183
00:12:51,496 --> 00:12:53,016
If they come back again,

184
00:12:53,055 --> 00:12:54,484
tell them,
I want to see them first.

185
00:12:54,509 --> 00:12:56,843
Now, let's get this show on the road.

186
00:12:57,331 --> 00:12:58,862
I'll get the tractor warmed up.

187
00:12:58,896 --> 00:13:00,942
Yeah, you do that.

188
00:13:07,550 --> 00:13:09,524
Look at him, will you?

189
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:15,505
He ain't had a hammer
in his hand in his whole life.

190
00:13:16,884 --> 00:13:18,415
What's up with the big cheese anyway?

191
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:21,296
I didn't think I'd see him out here
until the ribbon ceremony.

192
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,705
You know Mr. Krantz.

193
00:13:22,761 --> 00:13:24,728
He loves to micromanage.

194
00:13:24,835 --> 00:13:27,415
He wants you all to be on
the lookout for any Indian relics...

195
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,997
you might find in the next parcel.

196
00:13:29,022 --> 00:13:31,758
Maybe, he should come out with us
and survey and scout around a bit.

197
00:13:31,783 --> 00:13:32,814
Well, that's not gonna happen.

198
00:13:32,839 --> 00:13:34,246
He's not gonna get his ass
out of the trailer.

199
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,877
It's gonna be 110 in the shade.

200
00:13:35,914 --> 00:13:37,844
Meaning, the faster we get this done,

201
00:13:37,869 --> 00:13:39,078
the faster we get out of here.

202
00:13:39,103 --> 00:13:41,051
So, let's head out.

203
00:13:43,754 --> 00:13:46,293
Don't forget to check in later.

204
00:13:55,032 --> 00:13:56,627
Hello, Steve.

205
00:13:59,660 --> 00:14:01,327
Evans, go ahead.

206
00:14:01,352 --> 00:14:02,545
It's Jim here.

207
00:14:02,570 --> 00:14:06,088
I got the students all situated
pretty well out at the Krantz site.

208
00:14:06,113 --> 00:14:07,380
And I'm headed back.

209
00:14:07,405 --> 00:14:09,319
Any sign of Riley's truck?

210
00:14:09,344 --> 00:14:10,896
Uh, that's a negative.

211
00:14:10,921 --> 00:14:12,516
All right, well,
keep looking, will you?

212
00:14:12,541 --> 00:14:15,421
All right, I'll keep my eyes open.
See you later.

213
00:14:28,834 --> 00:14:31,048
Look at him, will you?

214
00:14:32,481 --> 00:14:34,973
I thought we were out here
to study archeology, not astronomy.

215
00:14:35,013 --> 00:14:36,686
Give him a break, Josh.

216
00:14:36,717 --> 00:14:39,169
Now, I want to see
the eclipse too when it happens.

217
00:14:39,217 --> 00:14:41,725
It's not gonna happen
for two more days, Rach.

218
00:14:41,784 --> 00:14:43,245
Right.

219
00:14:43,335 --> 00:14:45,150
Hey, Professor!

220
00:14:45,292 --> 00:14:47,028
You find something,
Mr. McMurphy?

221
00:14:47,060 --> 00:14:48,091
Um, not yet.

222
00:14:48,116 --> 00:14:50,365
I was just wondering
how the stars were looking.

223
00:14:50,405 --> 00:14:51,739
This morning.

224
00:14:51,778 --> 00:14:54,953
Your comedic talents
overwhelm me, Mr. McMurphy.

225
00:14:55,018 --> 00:14:56,184
I think you'd wanna...

226
00:14:56,209 --> 00:14:59,946
drop all your other courses and
concentrate solely on standup.

227
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:02,616
All right, Professor.
Just kidding.

228
00:15:02,641 --> 00:15:03,850
I know.

229
00:15:03,875 --> 00:15:06,057
But if I've taught you anything
over the last semester,

230
00:15:06,082 --> 00:15:08,366
it's that a good scientist
knows when to look down--

231
00:15:08,445 --> 00:15:10,048
And up.

232
00:15:10,342 --> 00:15:13,574
Hell, a major celestial event like this
won't take place again until...

233
00:15:13,599 --> 00:15:14,692
2078.

234
00:15:14,717 --> 00:15:16,394
I can wait.

235
00:15:16,743 --> 00:15:19,587
Is it true, this is the best place
to see it, Professor?

236
00:15:19,619 --> 00:15:20,913
According to the observatory,

237
00:15:20,938 --> 00:15:24,057
the optimum place for viewing the eclipse
is right here, in the Alabama hills.

238
00:15:24,082 --> 00:15:27,635
Hm, I guess that's why all
the motels in town were full up.

239
00:15:27,667 --> 00:15:29,114
It's history.

240
00:15:29,177 --> 00:15:31,668
Just like what you're digging
for here in the earth.

241
00:15:31,911 --> 00:15:34,303
When you three realize
all the sciences are...

242
00:15:34,343 --> 00:15:36,351
mutually bound together,

243
00:15:36,590 --> 00:15:38,977
you'll finally have learned
something meaningful.

244
00:15:39,677 --> 00:15:41,776
Now, keep working.

245
00:15:47,208 --> 00:15:48,208
Hey, Professor.

246
00:15:48,233 --> 00:15:49,838
Professor, wait a minute.
Check this out.

247
00:15:49,863 --> 00:15:50,870
What now, Mr. Cook?

248
00:15:50,895 --> 00:15:52,979
Hopefully, not more of
your would-be arrowheads.

249
00:15:53,004 --> 00:15:55,576
Oh, no, no, no.
This is something else.

250
00:16:00,984 --> 00:16:02,730
Man, that's weird.

251
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,127
What is it?

252
00:16:04,152 --> 00:16:06,638
- It's bones. I can tell you that.
- Keep brushing.

253
00:16:06,678 --> 00:16:09,067
Yes, by all means, Mr. Cook,
keep brushing.

254
00:16:17,580 --> 00:16:19,204
That's no dinosaur bone.

255
00:16:19,238 --> 00:16:21,238
It looks like a mammal.

256
00:16:21,325 --> 00:16:23,573
I think it's a femur.

257
00:16:24,591 --> 00:16:26,059
Oh, what?

258
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:29,591
Jeez, what was that?

259
00:16:29,745 --> 00:16:31,499
A tremor.

260
00:16:32,521 --> 00:16:35,308
I didn't know that
we were on a fault line.

261
00:16:35,371 --> 00:16:36,755
We're not.

262
00:16:38,545 --> 00:16:40,331
Oh!

263
00:16:44,034 --> 00:16:45,739
Is everyone okay?

264
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:47,397
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

265
00:16:47,422 --> 00:16:49,016
Yeah.

266
00:16:50,974 --> 00:16:52,742
Okay.

267
00:16:53,664 --> 00:16:55,695
Let's get back to work.

268
00:17:30,558 --> 00:17:32,427
Oh, my God!

269
00:17:37,069 --> 00:17:38,810
Run.

270
00:17:39,706 --> 00:17:41,643
Get to the jeep!

271
00:17:45,345 --> 00:17:46,984
Now!

272
00:18:02,596 --> 00:18:04,542
Oh, my God!

273
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:15,729
Oh, God!

274
00:18:15,754 --> 00:18:17,632
Oh, oh, please!

275
00:18:18,013 --> 00:18:19,101
Please!

276
00:18:19,149 --> 00:18:20,911
No, no!

277
00:18:23,176 --> 00:18:24,374
Please!

278
00:18:24,407 --> 00:18:26,200
Please, don't!

279
00:18:29,778 --> 00:18:31,659
Stop! No!

280
00:19:07,832 --> 00:19:10,432
Just in the nick of time.

281
00:19:22,535 --> 00:19:23,551
Excuse me, sir.

282
00:19:23,576 --> 00:19:25,046
There's a call on
the car phone for you, sir.

283
00:19:25,071 --> 00:19:27,498
All right. Take care of it.

284
00:20:01,412 --> 00:20:02,910
- Skipper.
- Hey.

285
00:20:02,935 --> 00:20:04,339
I'll give the place the once-over?

286
00:20:04,364 --> 00:20:05,897
Yeah.

287
00:20:05,961 --> 00:20:08,215
That's Pomeroy over there.

288
00:20:09,317 --> 00:20:11,862
Maybe, he knows something.

289
00:20:13,940 --> 00:20:16,954
Look, just make sure that
second quadrant is clear, okay?

290
00:20:18,470 --> 00:20:21,171
Sheriff, glad you're here.
I was just about to call you.

291
00:20:21,196 --> 00:20:22,956
It's about two missing men, right?

292
00:20:22,981 --> 00:20:24,695
Actually, three.

293
00:20:24,991 --> 00:20:26,515
Miller, Riley, and who else?

294
00:20:26,546 --> 00:20:29,438
A new kid, Chuck Hanson,
just came on the past week.

295
00:20:30,510 --> 00:20:32,065
Any idea what happened to them?

296
00:20:32,097 --> 00:20:33,637
Not a clue.

297
00:21:00,542 --> 00:21:02,193
Pomeroy.

298
00:21:03,167 --> 00:21:05,596
- What Sheriff got to say?
- Sheriff, this is Richard Krantz.

299
00:21:05,621 --> 00:21:07,552
- Sheriff.
- Mr. Krantz.

300
00:21:07,814 --> 00:21:10,390
It's a pleasure to meet
the man behind the curtain.

301
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,144
You got quite an operation here.

302
00:21:13,184 --> 00:21:15,360
It's just the beginning, Sheriff.

303
00:21:15,536 --> 00:21:18,569
This desert is gonna be
an oasis within two years.

304
00:21:18,805 --> 00:21:19,972
You wait.

305
00:21:20,011 --> 00:21:21,602
I'm sure you're right.

306
00:21:21,649 --> 00:21:24,856
Providing, your workers
don't keep disappearing.

307
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:28,145
So, they didn't make it
home either, I take it.

308
00:21:28,273 --> 00:21:29,759
No.

309
00:21:29,959 --> 00:21:31,753
You're working them
pretty hard, aren't you?

310
00:21:31,792 --> 00:21:33,792
I pay them well, Sheriff.

311
00:21:34,416 --> 00:21:36,455
You know, this may be
a little sensitive,

312
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,918
but uh...

313
00:21:38,334 --> 00:21:41,342
why don't you question the picketers
that are in front of your office?

314
00:21:41,367 --> 00:21:43,170
They're doing everything they can...

315
00:21:43,210 --> 00:21:45,012
to hold up this project.

316
00:21:45,044 --> 00:21:47,684
Oh, so you think
the Katonas are behind this?

317
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:49,540
No secrets about the threats.

318
00:21:49,574 --> 00:21:52,034
- Not to mention phone calls--
- Jimmy!

319
00:21:52,608 --> 00:21:53,920
Yes, sir.

320
00:21:55,199 --> 00:21:56,764
All I'm suggesting is...

321
00:21:56,789 --> 00:21:59,240
the Katonas have a definite motive.

322
00:21:59,414 --> 00:22:01,639
And you should, at least,
question them.

323
00:22:01,837 --> 00:22:05,194
Mr. Krantz, until I find
some evidence of foul play,

324
00:22:05,339 --> 00:22:07,456
I don't think I'm gonna do that.

325
00:22:09,903 --> 00:22:11,380
Sheriff.

326
00:22:12,726 --> 00:22:15,912
I found this out beyond
the construction perimeter in the brush.

327
00:22:15,937 --> 00:22:17,650
It's Miller's rifle.

328
00:22:18,759 --> 00:22:20,248
Along with this.

329
00:22:20,931 --> 00:22:22,466
Well,

330
00:22:22,791 --> 00:22:26,693
that should be enough evidence for you
to start an investigation, Sheriff.

331
00:22:26,756 --> 00:22:28,485
Mr. Krantz,
if it's all the same to you,

332
00:22:28,510 --> 00:22:31,090
you do your job
and let me do mine.

333
00:22:33,209 --> 00:22:34,683
Let's go.

334
00:22:39,153 --> 00:22:40,911
All right, Pomeroy.

335
00:22:40,967 --> 00:22:42,435
You're still pouring today, right?

336
00:22:42,460 --> 00:22:43,643
Yes, sir.

337
00:22:43,675 --> 00:22:46,786
All right, let's get the lead out.
We got some foundation to lay.

338
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:48,843
Mark, I want you
to bag that stuff up,

339
00:22:48,868 --> 00:22:50,545
drive it over to forensics
at county seat.

340
00:22:50,570 --> 00:22:52,130
Tell Coogan to put a priority on it.

341
00:22:52,155 --> 00:22:54,534
- Sure thing, boss.
- And call Sachetti at the impound.

342
00:22:54,566 --> 00:22:57,441
Tell him to tow those vehicles in
for a going-over.

343
00:22:57,708 --> 00:22:59,865
What do you think's going on?

344
00:23:00,250 --> 00:23:01,941
I don't know.
I'm not quite sure.

345
00:23:01,969 --> 00:23:04,536
But, I don't trust that guy.

346
00:23:06,483 --> 00:23:09,979
I think he knows a hell of
a lot more than he's telling.

347
00:23:10,062 --> 00:23:11,466
Where are you headed?

348
00:23:11,502 --> 00:23:14,474
Take a drive over to the reservation,
talk to Storm Cloud.

349
00:23:14,604 --> 00:23:15,748
Maybe, he knows something.

350
00:23:15,773 --> 00:23:17,788
Maybe, he does, Chief.

351
00:23:41,264 --> 00:23:42,400
Okay.

352
00:23:43,336 --> 00:23:44,616
Yeah.

353
00:23:44,641 --> 00:23:47,688
No, that's fine. It just means, I'm gonna
have to make three separate trips.

354
00:23:47,728 --> 00:23:49,759
Best get started then, Mikey.

355
00:23:49,825 --> 00:23:52,437
Sheriff wants those vehicles
towed in immediately.

356
00:23:53,115 --> 00:23:54,490
All right.

357
00:23:54,684 --> 00:23:56,855
I'll get on it right away, Mark.

358
00:24:00,558 --> 00:24:02,070
Right away.

359
00:24:03,333 --> 00:24:04,840
Almost.

360
00:24:16,521 --> 00:24:18,071
Well, well.

361
00:24:18,489 --> 00:24:20,230
When did you get back in town?

362
00:24:20,334 --> 00:24:22,151
This morning.

363
00:24:23,359 --> 00:24:24,981
This morning?

364
00:24:27,094 --> 00:24:28,429
I see.

365
00:24:29,408 --> 00:24:31,075
What took so long?

366
00:24:31,464 --> 00:24:32,916
- Things.
- Oh.

367
00:24:34,388 --> 00:24:35,809
I see.

368
00:24:36,388 --> 00:24:39,323
And uh, so now, you're back
for the whole summer?

369
00:24:40,123 --> 00:24:41,701
Apparently.

370
00:24:42,710 --> 00:24:44,194
Wow.

371
00:24:45,284 --> 00:24:47,724
Do you have anything
you want to say to me?

372
00:24:48,562 --> 00:24:50,181
Yeah.

373
00:24:50,365 --> 00:24:52,740
Yeah, actually,
as a matter of fact, I do.

374
00:24:52,898 --> 00:24:55,024
I missed you.

375
00:24:57,737 --> 00:24:59,271
Me too.

376
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:20,397
You make no sense at all.

377
00:25:20,437 --> 00:25:22,233
Advancing our cause doesn't mean...

378
00:25:22,265 --> 00:25:24,081
you have to be belligerent
with everyone...

379
00:25:24,106 --> 00:25:25,273
who disagrees with you.

380
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:28,351
I only want what's right
for our people and us, Kaya.

381
00:25:28,382 --> 00:25:29,970
That's just it, Black Hawk.

382
00:25:30,001 --> 00:25:31,373
There is no "us".

383
00:25:31,398 --> 00:25:32,623
There never was.

384
00:25:32,648 --> 00:25:33,686
What do you mean?

385
00:25:33,711 --> 00:25:35,877
I don't wish to be a part
of your militant stance...

386
00:25:35,917 --> 00:25:37,439
with the townspeople.

387
00:25:37,464 --> 00:25:39,599
Now, you talk like your grandfather.

388
00:25:39,646 --> 00:25:40,865
Weak,

389
00:25:40,897 --> 00:25:42,039
tired,

390
00:25:42,079 --> 00:25:44,725
unwilling to stand up for our rights.

391
00:25:44,792 --> 00:25:46,459
If the white man has
taught us anything,

392
00:25:46,484 --> 00:25:48,444
it's that we must fight
for what we want.

393
00:25:48,498 --> 00:25:50,507
Yes, fight.

394
00:25:51,131 --> 00:25:53,805
But I do not like
how you do battle.

395
00:26:04,542 --> 00:26:06,043
Well, hello, Sheriff.

396
00:26:06,068 --> 00:26:07,200
Kaya.

397
00:26:07,225 --> 00:26:08,598
You come to arrest us all today?

398
00:26:08,637 --> 00:26:10,155
No, nothing like that.

399
00:26:10,182 --> 00:26:12,500
Just need some questions
answered is all.

400
00:26:12,603 --> 00:26:13,955
Is your grandfather home?

401
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:15,257
He's just starting sweat lodge.

402
00:26:15,282 --> 00:26:16,336
Oh.

403
00:26:16,370 --> 00:26:18,101
Um, I can come back later.

404
00:26:18,126 --> 00:26:19,491
Oh, no, please,
I'm sure he'll see you.

405
00:26:19,516 --> 00:26:20,856
- Come.
- Yeah?

406
00:26:20,952 --> 00:26:22,388
All right.

407
00:26:30,015 --> 00:26:32,268
So, how's your teaching
been this semester?

408
00:26:32,293 --> 00:26:33,693
It's okay, I guess.

409
00:26:33,733 --> 00:26:35,016
It's been a bit tough.

410
00:26:35,050 --> 00:26:36,499
With the cuts in federal funding,

411
00:26:36,524 --> 00:26:38,443
we've had to combine a lot of classes.

412
00:26:38,468 --> 00:26:41,031
But, you know,
students have adapted well.

413
00:26:41,118 --> 00:26:44,574
Maybe, you folks should think about
opening a casino around here.

414
00:26:44,599 --> 00:26:46,959
Mm, Grandfather doesn't
believe in them.

415
00:26:46,999 --> 00:26:48,919
- Yeah.
- He says they weaken the spirit.

416
00:26:48,966 --> 00:26:52,391
Maybe so, but it sure would
bring in some much-needed revenue.

417
00:26:52,518 --> 00:26:56,407
It would also bring drunkenness,
prostitution, and crime.

418
00:26:56,541 --> 00:26:59,276
Oh, good morning to you,
Storm Cloud.

419
00:26:59,805 --> 00:27:02,524
Sheriff Evans is here to ask you
some questions, Grandfather.

420
00:27:02,549 --> 00:27:04,075
I didn't think you'd mind.

421
00:27:04,123 --> 00:27:07,495
Running Wolf,
it is always good to see a brother.

422
00:27:08,819 --> 00:27:11,240
Haven't heard that name in awhile.

423
00:27:11,748 --> 00:27:14,065
Well maybe, you should
use it more often.

424
00:27:14,304 --> 00:27:16,616
I might, if I could only
convince people to get beyond...

425
00:27:16,641 --> 00:27:18,331
the color of my hair and eyes.

426
00:27:18,385 --> 00:27:21,073
One just needs to look at
your beautiful daughter...

427
00:27:21,104 --> 00:27:23,271
to know that your bloodline runs strong.

428
00:27:23,296 --> 00:27:24,481
So, how is Kelly?

429
00:27:24,506 --> 00:27:25,567
She's fine.

430
00:27:25,592 --> 00:27:27,398
She's got back in town today.

431
00:27:27,431 --> 00:27:30,065
She has the spirit of the Katona.

432
00:27:30,328 --> 00:27:31,947
And her mother's attitude.

433
00:27:31,972 --> 00:27:33,466
She's young.

434
00:27:33,601 --> 00:27:34,910
Come.

435
00:27:36,727 --> 00:27:38,899
Well, if you'll excuse me,
I must be going, Sheriff.

436
00:27:38,924 --> 00:27:40,589
My next class is at 11:00.

437
00:27:40,645 --> 00:27:42,343
Thank you, Kaya.

438
00:27:50,460 --> 00:27:54,228
You have come about the incident
at the worksite, have you not?

439
00:27:55,035 --> 00:27:56,747
Yes, that's right.

440
00:27:56,858 --> 00:27:58,096
How did you know?

441
00:27:58,135 --> 00:28:00,044
I heard about it earlier.

442
00:28:00,456 --> 00:28:01,587
From who?

443
00:28:01,635 --> 00:28:03,134
Chinkana.

444
00:28:03,293 --> 00:28:04,976
Chinkana.

445
00:28:06,019 --> 00:28:07,352
Don't know him.

446
00:28:07,413 --> 00:28:09,582
It's Indian for grapevine.

447
00:28:12,040 --> 00:28:14,484
Yes, three men have gone missing.

448
00:28:15,278 --> 00:28:18,512
And you think that someone here
may be responsible?

449
00:28:18,575 --> 00:28:20,011
Maybe,

450
00:28:20,118 --> 00:28:21,737
maybe not.

451
00:28:22,174 --> 00:28:25,143
There have been threats made
by some of the picketers.

452
00:28:25,280 --> 00:28:28,670
Angry words don't always
lead to violence.

453
00:28:28,718 --> 00:28:30,234
Three men are missing,

454
00:28:30,259 --> 00:28:33,404
but I didn't say
anything about violence.

455
00:28:34,638 --> 00:28:36,136
If you know something,
Storm Cloud--

456
00:28:36,161 --> 00:28:38,062
I know that that's why you're here.

457
00:28:38,134 --> 00:28:40,071
To accuse one of us.

458
00:28:40,125 --> 00:28:42,134
This is just a follow-up.

459
00:28:43,241 --> 00:28:46,500
None of our people set foot
on that ground last night.

460
00:28:46,952 --> 00:28:49,588
And neither should anyone else.

461
00:28:49,842 --> 00:28:52,488
What happened to
those men was a sign.

462
00:28:52,750 --> 00:28:54,420
The construction must stop.

463
00:28:54,468 --> 00:28:56,928
With all due respect, Storm Cloud,

464
00:28:57,337 --> 00:28:59,519
that land is not...

465
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:01,323
on the Katona Reservation.

466
00:29:01,363 --> 00:29:03,786
Still, it is on unholy land.

467
00:29:03,811 --> 00:29:05,282
Okay, listen to me.

468
00:29:05,306 --> 00:29:07,019
I was out there just this morning.

469
00:29:07,044 --> 00:29:08,873
There is nothing there to indicate...

470
00:29:08,898 --> 00:29:11,416
that your ancestors were ever there.

471
00:29:11,448 --> 00:29:13,693
Our ancestors, Running Wolf.

472
00:29:13,718 --> 00:29:15,416
Our ancestors!

473
00:29:15,614 --> 00:29:17,662
Have you forgotten
that your grandfather,

474
00:29:17,687 --> 00:29:20,626
a great chief, is buried
on this reservation?

475
00:29:25,340 --> 00:29:27,599
No, I haven't.

476
00:29:27,853 --> 00:29:29,895
You must never forget.

477
00:29:29,975 --> 00:29:33,689
The blood of the chiefs also flows
inside of you, Running Wolf.

478
00:29:33,721 --> 00:29:36,692
It's what gives you
the strength over evil.

479
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:43,184
I, I understand that, Storm Cloud.

480
00:29:44,975 --> 00:29:46,828
But being sheriff...

481
00:29:46,978 --> 00:29:51,184
allows me to extend
that power for the good of all.

482
00:29:53,245 --> 00:29:54,460
Then know that...

483
00:29:54,485 --> 00:29:57,104
whatever lies out beyond our borders...

484
00:29:57,136 --> 00:29:59,281
should be left undisturbed...

485
00:29:59,958 --> 00:30:02,067
for the sake of all.

486
00:30:16,417 --> 00:30:18,504
Well, half-breed.

487
00:30:19,332 --> 00:30:21,618
Who do you serve today, hmm?

488
00:30:21,892 --> 00:30:23,448
Indian?

489
00:30:23,922 --> 00:30:25,599
Or white man?

490
00:30:28,050 --> 00:30:29,499
Both.

491
00:30:29,991 --> 00:30:31,598
Equally.

492
00:30:32,064 --> 00:30:34,249
If only it were the truth.

493
00:31:11,215 --> 00:31:13,743
Dude, I say, we call it a day.

494
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:17,208
We got about another hour
of daylight left.

495
00:31:17,233 --> 00:31:19,297
Let's just go ahead
and knock it off, though.

496
00:31:19,322 --> 00:31:21,186
Then we don't have
to come back tomorrow, okay?

497
00:31:21,211 --> 00:31:22,795
Whatever.

498
00:31:24,674 --> 00:31:27,579
Hey, Lou, go ahead and move to
your left about a foot, would you?

499
00:31:27,604 --> 00:31:31,063
All right, but let's make this quick.
I'm toast already on one side.

500
00:31:31,219 --> 00:31:33,952
Whoa!
Hey, hey, hey!

501
00:31:35,150 --> 00:31:37,158
What was that?

502
00:31:40,507 --> 00:31:42,888
What the hell are you guys
doing down there?

503
00:31:42,991 --> 00:31:44,484
You didn't feel that up there?

504
00:31:44,516 --> 00:31:45,575
Feel what?

505
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,480
We had a serious earthquake
just hit us down here.

506
00:31:47,505 --> 00:31:48,634
You didn't feel it?

507
00:31:48,659 --> 00:31:50,102
Come on, quit fooling around, you guys.

508
00:31:50,127 --> 00:31:53,078
Let's just get this thing done.
I didn't feel anything.

509
00:31:58,372 --> 00:32:01,145
Okay. Um, hey, Lou,
do me a favor and...

510
00:32:01,170 --> 00:32:04,177
move forward about, uh,
about three feet.

511
00:32:04,671 --> 00:32:06,548
That's more like it.

512
00:32:10,544 --> 00:32:11,653
Whoa! What?

513
00:32:11,678 --> 00:32:13,472
No!

514
00:32:13,967 --> 00:32:15,316
What the hell?

515
00:32:15,356 --> 00:32:16,904
Dave.

516
00:32:17,054 --> 00:32:19,462
- Dave!
- What the hell is that?

517
00:32:26,668 --> 00:32:29,145
Let's get out of here, man.
Come on!

518
00:34:15,420 --> 00:34:18,140
Holy, holy shit!

519
00:35:48,403 --> 00:35:50,536
Step forward, warrior.

520
00:35:56,974 --> 00:35:59,580
You have seen the Bone Eater.

521
00:35:59,695 --> 00:36:01,357
It has risen.

522
00:36:02,007 --> 00:36:04,901
And the sacred moon
will soon obscure the sun.

523
00:36:05,107 --> 00:36:06,643
Time is short.

524
00:36:06,897 --> 00:36:09,486
I must know its secret
before it's too late.

525
00:36:09,621 --> 00:36:11,299
There is no secret.

526
00:36:11,363 --> 00:36:12,768
Only death.

527
00:36:12,800 --> 00:36:15,204
They brought this demon
onto themselves.

528
00:36:15,275 --> 00:36:18,405
But, we can use it
to our own advantage.

529
00:36:18,552 --> 00:36:19,695
No.

530
00:36:19,758 --> 00:36:22,919
The Bone Eater is
an enemy of all life,

531
00:36:22,950 --> 00:36:24,788
not just the white man.

532
00:36:24,946 --> 00:36:28,301
Once all six renegades
have been resurrected,

533
00:36:28,386 --> 00:36:30,825
the creature will be unstoppable.

534
00:36:31,008 --> 00:36:33,029
You must find the bone axe.

535
00:36:33,097 --> 00:36:36,704
The creature must be destroyed
before the six become one.

536
00:36:36,759 --> 00:36:39,105
If you're too afraid
to wield that power,

537
00:36:39,169 --> 00:36:41,145
then tell me of this sacred weapon.

538
00:36:41,185 --> 00:36:43,037
I will find it myself.

539
00:36:43,267 --> 00:36:46,032
Now, who is being foolish?

540
00:36:46,289 --> 00:36:48,278
Once the eclipse has completed,

541
00:36:48,322 --> 00:36:51,029
it will take the will
of the gods to destroy it.

542
00:36:51,116 --> 00:36:52,894
I don't believe you.

543
00:36:53,033 --> 00:36:54,954
With the creature as our ally,

544
00:36:54,979 --> 00:36:57,757
we could drive the white man
from all of our land.

545
00:36:57,867 --> 00:37:00,777
Restore our people to prominence!

546
00:37:00,831 --> 00:37:03,400
Anger clouds you, Black Hawk.

547
00:37:03,502 --> 00:37:06,719
You cannot befriend evil
to do your bidding.

548
00:37:06,783 --> 00:37:08,751
There must be a way.

549
00:37:09,200 --> 00:37:11,448
And I will soon discover it,

550
00:37:12,788 --> 00:37:15,307
with or without your help.

551
00:37:29,846 --> 00:37:30,981
Hey, Kelly.

552
00:37:31,006 --> 00:37:33,004
Turn the music down, will you?
I'm on the phone.

553
00:37:33,029 --> 00:37:34,612
All right!

554
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:36,506
I'm sorry, Sal.

555
00:37:36,537 --> 00:37:38,188
If you don't mind,
could you repeat that?

556
00:37:38,220 --> 00:37:39,558
Yeah, no problem.

557
00:37:39,597 --> 00:37:43,432
I said I found traces of crystallized
blood and bone samples...

558
00:37:43,457 --> 00:37:45,448
embedded in the cloth you sent me.

559
00:37:45,535 --> 00:37:46,931
What does that mean?

560
00:37:46,956 --> 00:37:48,050
Well, for that to happen,

561
00:37:48,075 --> 00:37:51,767
the victim would have had to have
fallen straight into a blast furnace.

562
00:37:51,859 --> 00:37:54,402
Well, there's nothing
like that out there.

563
00:37:54,450 --> 00:37:56,523
And here's something
for Sherlock Holmes:

564
00:37:56,587 --> 00:38:00,940
The shirt itself shows absolutely
no signs of being burned.

565
00:38:01,024 --> 00:38:03,127
Could the blood samples
have been introduced...

566
00:38:03,152 --> 00:38:05,006
into the cloth sometime later?

567
00:38:05,031 --> 00:38:06,774
Not a chance.

568
00:38:07,139 --> 00:38:08,480
You sure about that?

569
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:10,405
I'd stake my pension on it.

570
00:38:10,985 --> 00:38:12,161
Well, thanks, Sal.

571
00:38:12,186 --> 00:38:14,113
As usual, you've ruined my day.

572
00:38:14,145 --> 00:38:15,622
Sorry, Steve.

573
00:38:15,657 --> 00:38:18,039
I'll send you some free aspirin,
on the county.

574
00:38:18,070 --> 00:38:20,483
Yeah, I'll be looking for it.

575
00:38:26,808 --> 00:38:29,269
Come on, Dad,
nobody does that anymore.

576
00:38:29,309 --> 00:38:31,087
Ah, well, I guess
I'm getting old, Kel.

577
00:38:31,113 --> 00:38:33,563
Where are you going
all made up like that?

578
00:38:33,616 --> 00:38:35,764
I'm going up
to Big Pine to see a movie.

579
00:38:35,801 --> 00:38:37,440
Tonight?

580
00:38:37,911 --> 00:38:40,596
We haven't spent
two minutes together.

581
00:38:41,573 --> 00:38:43,487
We have all summer, right?

582
00:38:43,556 --> 00:38:45,155
Yeah.

583
00:38:45,501 --> 00:38:48,063
I, I don't want you going up
to Big Pine tonight.

584
00:38:48,180 --> 00:38:50,580
What's the big deal?
It's just a date.

585
00:38:50,668 --> 00:38:52,348
With who?

586
00:38:54,236 --> 00:38:56,444
It's not that Sachetti kid, is it?

587
00:38:56,481 --> 00:38:57,671
What if it is?

588
00:38:57,696 --> 00:38:59,259
He's too old for you.

589
00:38:59,290 --> 00:39:01,740
Dad, he's just 21.

590
00:39:02,056 --> 00:39:05,587
Well, four years at your age
is a, is a lot of difference.

591
00:39:05,687 --> 00:39:07,847
Mom is four years younger than you.

592
00:39:07,887 --> 00:39:09,405
It's not the same thing.

593
00:39:09,437 --> 00:39:10,869
It is to me.

594
00:39:10,909 --> 00:39:12,702
I can handle myself!

595
00:39:12,780 --> 00:39:15,400
Yeah, well, that's just
what I'm afraid of.

596
00:39:15,844 --> 00:39:17,241
Look.

597
00:39:17,305 --> 00:39:20,935
Um, can't you just humor
your old man once?

598
00:39:21,062 --> 00:39:22,481
And stick around?

599
00:39:22,522 --> 00:39:24,714
No, I'll be back later.

600
00:39:24,761 --> 00:39:26,374
No, you'll be back at 11:00.

601
00:39:26,406 --> 00:39:28,075
Dad, I'm 17.

602
00:39:28,115 --> 00:39:30,649
My house, my rules.

603
00:39:30,816 --> 00:39:31,991
11:00.

604
00:39:32,039 --> 00:39:33,483
Whatever.

605
00:39:38,222 --> 00:39:40,061
Great.

606
00:39:49,437 --> 00:39:50,532
Let me get this straight.

607
00:39:50,557 --> 00:39:53,277
You just compromised
your integrity for money?

608
00:39:53,447 --> 00:39:55,959
What he's doing is wrong,
Dad, and you know it.

609
00:39:55,984 --> 00:39:57,903
Look, don't lecture me
on what's right and wrong, all right?

610
00:39:57,928 --> 00:40:00,482
That money is putting your ass
through engineering school.

611
00:40:00,731 --> 00:40:03,377
You don't want it? You wanna spend
the rest of your life digging ditches?

612
00:40:03,442 --> 00:40:06,623
- That's fine with me.
- Money isn't everything, Pop.

613
00:40:07,016 --> 00:40:09,049
And I'd rather you not sell
your soul to Krantz...

614
00:40:09,074 --> 00:40:11,417
just to put me through college.

615
00:40:12,020 --> 00:40:13,814
Look, son.

616
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:16,935
It's easy to have high morals
when you're 22.

617
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:19,070
But at my age,

618
00:40:19,102 --> 00:40:20,696
how am I gonna start over?

619
00:40:20,721 --> 00:40:23,033
A man like Krantz has the power to...

620
00:40:23,183 --> 00:40:25,001
ruin me for the rest of my life.

621
00:40:25,037 --> 00:40:27,782
Only 'cause you gave it to him, Dad.

622
00:40:45,198 --> 00:40:46,943
Kaya.

623
00:40:47,215 --> 00:40:48,395
Is everything okay?

624
00:40:48,420 --> 00:40:50,016
I hope it's not too late.

625
00:40:50,045 --> 00:40:51,550
No, not at all.

626
00:40:51,622 --> 00:40:53,812
Uh, please, come in.

627
00:40:58,944 --> 00:41:00,555
Anything I can get you?

628
00:41:00,584 --> 00:41:02,601
No, thank you. I'm fine.

629
00:41:05,144 --> 00:41:07,358
So, what brings you over?

630
00:41:07,667 --> 00:41:09,064
Look, Steve.

631
00:41:09,143 --> 00:41:11,100
I know why you were
at the reservation earlier.

632
00:41:11,155 --> 00:41:12,719
It's those missing men.

633
00:41:12,750 --> 00:41:14,683
Storm Cloud sent you, didn't he?

634
00:41:14,936 --> 00:41:18,050
I, I felt that he was
holding something back.

635
00:41:18,075 --> 00:41:20,267
No, no, I came on my own.

636
00:41:20,519 --> 00:41:21,951
Look, Kaya.

637
00:41:22,189 --> 00:41:25,605
All evidence points to the fact
that these men are dead.

638
00:41:25,748 --> 00:41:28,357
Now, if you know something,
you need to tell me.

639
00:41:28,547 --> 00:41:31,214
Well, it's not something
you're gonna want to hear.

640
00:41:32,165 --> 00:41:34,107
It's Black Hawk, isn't it?

641
00:41:35,210 --> 00:41:36,615
No.

642
00:41:40,434 --> 00:41:42,982
Have you ever heard the legend
of the Bone Eater?

643
00:41:43,404 --> 00:41:44,938
Yeah.

644
00:41:45,327 --> 00:41:47,549
The curse of Torak.

645
00:41:48,384 --> 00:41:50,354
Yeah, my older brother
used to spook me...

646
00:41:50,379 --> 00:41:52,382
by telling me scary stories about it.

647
00:41:52,425 --> 00:41:55,665
Well, according to Storm Cloud,
the legend is true.

648
00:41:55,900 --> 00:41:57,840
- Come on.
- Two centuries ago,

649
00:41:57,871 --> 00:42:00,001
the Katona tribe and
white settlers alike...

650
00:42:00,026 --> 00:42:02,532
were menaced by a band
of six renegades...

651
00:42:02,571 --> 00:42:05,393
led by a young shaman named Torak.

652
00:42:05,464 --> 00:42:06,905
Yeah.

653
00:42:07,303 --> 00:42:09,349
He was bypassed as rightful chief,

654
00:42:09,374 --> 00:42:10,946
so he broke from the tribe, right?

655
00:42:10,971 --> 00:42:14,052
They harmed so many
in their quest for power,

656
00:42:14,083 --> 00:42:16,201
engaging in ritualistic murder,

657
00:42:16,232 --> 00:42:17,883
even cannibalism.

658
00:42:17,980 --> 00:42:21,546
It took several medicine men
and many warriors...

659
00:42:21,571 --> 00:42:24,228
to finally surround the six
and destroy them.

660
00:42:24,303 --> 00:42:26,356
They were buried unceremoniously...

661
00:42:26,381 --> 00:42:28,744
in the same area where,
30 years ago,

662
00:42:28,769 --> 00:42:32,700
a group of miners uncovered
the sacred bone axe.

663
00:42:36,172 --> 00:42:39,271
Tragically, the creature
awoke from its slumber.

664
00:42:39,302 --> 00:42:41,948
The men were pierced
with shards of sharp bone,

665
00:42:41,972 --> 00:42:43,750
disintegrating them.

666
00:42:49,609 --> 00:42:52,075
Before the miners realized
what they had done,

667
00:42:52,123 --> 00:42:54,099
it was too late.

668
00:42:58,173 --> 00:43:01,377
One of them was able to pierce
the creature with the sacred bone axe,

669
00:43:01,402 --> 00:43:03,346
sending it back into the earth.

670
00:43:03,385 --> 00:43:06,610
But unfortunately,
none of them survived.

671
00:43:14,388 --> 00:43:16,253
By building on that land,

672
00:43:16,301 --> 00:43:18,801
Krantz has desecrated
the sacred ground...

673
00:43:18,837 --> 00:43:21,896
and once again
awakened the Bone Eater.

674
00:43:22,021 --> 00:43:25,586
That is why Storm Cloud
wanted the ground left alone.

675
00:43:25,673 --> 00:43:27,963
Kaya, this is the 21st century.

676
00:43:27,988 --> 00:43:30,051
I can't act on legend.

677
00:43:30,099 --> 00:43:32,307
These are evil spirits...

678
00:43:32,332 --> 00:43:36,229
that were sealed in the earth
eternally with a sacred war axe.

679
00:43:36,263 --> 00:43:38,088
Yeah, yeah.

680
00:43:38,152 --> 00:43:40,692
And before he died,
Torak cursed his killers,

681
00:43:40,717 --> 00:43:43,511
saying that his bones and
the bones of his brothers...

682
00:43:43,551 --> 00:43:47,070
would rise up like a demon
and take revenge.

683
00:43:47,196 --> 00:43:50,332
Right after the ghost
of Christmas past.

684
00:43:51,153 --> 00:43:53,586
I should not have come.

685
00:43:54,904 --> 00:43:57,011
Oh, Kaya, I'm sorry.

686
00:43:57,036 --> 00:43:58,655
Listen.

687
00:43:59,875 --> 00:44:01,082
Please, please.

688
00:44:01,122 --> 00:44:02,638
Forgive me?

689
00:44:02,979 --> 00:44:04,943
It's just that I've got
three men missing,

690
00:44:04,968 --> 00:44:06,585
presumed dead,
and I can't go...

691
00:44:06,610 --> 00:44:09,126
to these people's families
with legends of bone creatures.

692
00:44:09,157 --> 00:44:11,286
Steve, this demon lives.

693
00:44:11,316 --> 00:44:13,897
We are in great danger.

694
00:44:15,224 --> 00:44:16,897
Kaya,

695
00:44:18,126 --> 00:44:20,037
for what it's worth,

696
00:44:20,408 --> 00:44:23,386
thank you for coming over here
and telling me this.

697
00:44:24,198 --> 00:44:27,961
It's only worth something
if you listen.

698
00:44:42,895 --> 00:44:45,507
Now, just for a few minutes, okay?

699
00:44:45,777 --> 00:44:47,016
Relax, Lol.

700
00:44:47,049 --> 00:44:49,025
Nothing's gonna happen.

701
00:44:49,749 --> 00:44:51,678
Well, maybe something.

702
00:44:51,726 --> 00:44:54,173
Yeah, if you're lucky.

703
00:44:54,993 --> 00:44:56,820
I got something for you.

704
00:44:56,889 --> 00:45:00,202
Yeah, I got a good idea
what it is too.

705
00:45:00,337 --> 00:45:02,688
No, really.

706
00:45:03,117 --> 00:45:04,411
Here.

707
00:45:04,466 --> 00:45:06,643
Oh, my God, Dex.

708
00:45:06,698 --> 00:45:08,780
You're so sweet.

709
00:45:08,978 --> 00:45:10,256
What is it?

710
00:45:10,288 --> 00:45:12,153
That? Go ahead and open it.

711
00:45:15,571 --> 00:45:17,773
I can't believe it.

712
00:45:18,265 --> 00:45:19,988
It's so beautiful.

713
00:45:20,076 --> 00:45:21,505
Where did you get this?

714
00:45:21,537 --> 00:45:22,870
At the site.

715
00:45:23,035 --> 00:45:24,308
You're kidding me.

716
00:45:24,363 --> 00:45:27,172
No, no. There's tons
of great stuff out there.

717
00:45:27,644 --> 00:45:29,438
When I saw that,

718
00:45:29,584 --> 00:45:31,907
I knew it was meant for you.

719
00:45:33,132 --> 00:45:36,519
Took it to the town jeweler,
had him shine it up like new.

720
00:45:37,112 --> 00:45:39,241
You're the best.

721
00:45:46,465 --> 00:45:47,561
Here, wait.

722
00:45:47,632 --> 00:45:49,418
Let's see what it looks like.

723
00:45:55,501 --> 00:45:57,089
So, what do you think?

724
00:45:57,144 --> 00:45:58,795
It's beautiful.

725
00:45:58,875 --> 00:46:00,628
Just like you.

726
00:46:11,888 --> 00:46:13,563
What was that?

727
00:46:14,462 --> 00:46:16,036
I don't know.

728
00:46:23,069 --> 00:46:25,219
Run, Lolli, run!

729
00:47:04,125 --> 00:47:05,468
Hello.

730
00:47:09,538 --> 00:47:11,266
Hello, Kelly?

731
00:47:47,874 --> 00:47:49,091
He's gonna kill me.

732
00:47:49,128 --> 00:47:51,353
No, he won't.
You have a legitimate excuse.

733
00:47:51,400 --> 00:47:53,083
Yeah, well.

734
00:47:54,917 --> 00:47:56,865
What's wrong with you?

735
00:47:57,991 --> 00:47:59,389
I don't know.

736
00:48:00,267 --> 00:48:01,830
You just get in here today,

737
00:48:01,870 --> 00:48:04,171
and I'm already thinking
about you going back.

738
00:48:05,100 --> 00:48:06,468
Don't.

739
00:48:08,749 --> 00:48:10,765
Why don't you just stay?

740
00:48:10,983 --> 00:48:12,525
And live where?

741
00:48:12,549 --> 00:48:13,946
With my father?

742
00:48:13,976 --> 00:48:17,069
We'll be lucky if we make it
through the summer in one piece.

743
00:48:17,917 --> 00:48:19,601
So, come live with me.

744
00:48:20,217 --> 00:48:22,926
Do you want to be
the one to tell him that?

745
00:48:25,028 --> 00:48:26,512
No, thanks.

746
00:48:27,730 --> 00:48:29,027
Jeez! Ah--

747
00:48:29,067 --> 00:48:30,932
It's so late. I gotta go in.

748
00:48:31,011 --> 00:48:32,516
Do you want me to come in
with you, try to explain?

749
00:48:32,541 --> 00:48:33,704
No, no, no.

750
00:48:33,729 --> 00:48:36,007
I think it's better if I do it myself.

751
00:48:36,032 --> 00:48:37,596
Where is my purse?

752
00:48:37,636 --> 00:48:39,771
Uh, I think you left it
in the back seat.

753
00:48:39,815 --> 00:48:41,731
What's that?

754
00:48:42,572 --> 00:48:44,288
That?
Oh, I don't know.

755
00:48:44,313 --> 00:48:46,518
It's some old tomahawk or something.

756
00:48:46,551 --> 00:48:49,162
I found it, uh, lying around
the lot this afternoon.

757
00:48:49,273 --> 00:48:50,633
Now.

758
00:48:51,373 --> 00:48:53,585
Why don't you slide
over here a minute?

759
00:48:59,866 --> 00:49:01,311
Oh, Jeez!

760
00:49:01,336 --> 00:49:02,365
Okay, you have to go.

761
00:49:02,390 --> 00:49:03,606
Okay, okay. Hey...

762
00:49:03,654 --> 00:49:05,059
call me tomorrow.

763
00:49:05,161 --> 00:49:06,655
Okay, pst!

764
00:49:06,687 --> 00:49:08,306
Drive.

765
00:49:19,358 --> 00:49:21,561
Do you know what time it is,
young lady?

766
00:49:21,767 --> 00:49:23,116
Late, I know.

767
00:49:23,141 --> 00:49:25,158
It's 3:15 A.M.

768
00:49:25,187 --> 00:49:27,280
That is beyond late.

769
00:49:31,071 --> 00:49:35,008
Kelly, I thought I told you
to get back home before 11:00.

770
00:49:35,059 --> 00:49:36,455
I would have been, Dad.

771
00:49:36,480 --> 00:49:39,497
But, there was a huge accident
on the other side of the county line.

772
00:49:39,545 --> 00:49:41,071
Come on.

773
00:49:41,135 --> 00:49:43,484
That kind of BS doesn't
cut it with me anymore.

774
00:49:43,540 --> 00:49:44,880
I'm not lying.

775
00:49:44,905 --> 00:49:46,309
Look, if you don't start
telling the truth,

776
00:49:46,334 --> 00:49:48,887
you can forget about ever seeing
that Sachetti kid again.

777
00:49:48,912 --> 00:49:50,841
You can't tell me who I can date.

778
00:49:50,875 --> 00:49:53,829
When you're in my house,
I sure as hell can!

779
00:49:54,345 --> 00:49:55,864
Look, Dad.

780
00:49:55,921 --> 00:49:57,967
There really was an accident, okay?

781
00:49:57,992 --> 00:49:59,684
Traffic was backed up for miles.

782
00:49:59,708 --> 00:50:01,797
I'm surprised they didn't call you.

783
00:50:01,902 --> 00:50:03,773
Yeah, me too.

784
00:50:10,797 --> 00:50:11,981
Yeah, Evans here.

785
00:50:12,036 --> 00:50:13,496
Hey, boss, sorry to wake you.

786
00:50:13,521 --> 00:50:14,687
It's Roberts.

787
00:50:14,735 --> 00:50:16,040
That's okay, buddy.

788
00:50:16,096 --> 00:50:17,579
I was up.

789
00:50:18,706 --> 00:50:20,645
I just got a call from Burns
down at the station.

790
00:50:20,670 --> 00:50:23,153
He got a dispatch from highway patrol
about a truck accident...

791
00:50:23,178 --> 00:50:24,916
a couple hours ago,
up near Big Pine.

792
00:50:24,952 --> 00:50:26,957
Yeah, Kelly was just
telling me about it.

793
00:50:27,009 --> 00:50:29,364
Sheriff, there's something else.

794
00:50:29,700 --> 00:50:31,652
A vehicle was found
smashed to pieces...

795
00:50:31,677 --> 00:50:34,274
up on Krantz's property
near the site.

796
00:50:34,861 --> 00:50:36,631
How does it affect us?

797
00:50:36,923 --> 00:50:39,022
They found a purse
on the side of the road.

798
00:50:39,091 --> 00:50:41,133
Sheriff, it's Lolli's.

799
00:50:43,760 --> 00:50:45,218
You're sure about that?

800
00:50:45,276 --> 00:50:47,259
Yeah, they found her County ID
inside the wallet.

801
00:50:47,284 --> 00:50:48,832
They called us right away.

802
00:50:48,912 --> 00:50:50,309
Right. Uh...

803
00:50:50,380 --> 00:50:52,311
I'll, I'll go check it out.

804
00:50:52,359 --> 00:50:54,361
Sheriff, if it's okay,
I'd like to go.

805
00:50:54,415 --> 00:50:56,941
Yeah, I'll, uh, see you out there.

806
00:50:59,742 --> 00:51:00,925
What was that about?

807
00:51:00,973 --> 00:51:02,734
Nothing, it's just routine.

808
00:51:03,123 --> 00:51:05,059
Now, who's BSing?

809
00:51:06,913 --> 00:51:08,556
I'm sorry, honey.

810
00:51:08,739 --> 00:51:09,909
I really am.

811
00:51:09,941 --> 00:51:12,107
I shouldn't have doubted you.

812
00:51:12,801 --> 00:51:15,097
So, what's really the matter?

813
00:51:16,177 --> 00:51:18,283
Lolli may have been hurt.

814
00:51:19,100 --> 00:51:20,982
I'll call you when I know more.

815
00:51:21,037 --> 00:51:22,497
Okay?

816
00:51:31,959 --> 00:51:33,972
Hank, you got any of this
figured out yet?

817
00:51:34,023 --> 00:51:35,356
Not yet, Steve.

818
00:51:35,434 --> 00:51:37,642
But it's the damnedest thing
I've ever seen.

819
00:51:38,207 --> 00:51:39,887
The skid marks are here,

820
00:51:39,934 --> 00:51:42,545
yet the truck's over 100 feet away.

821
00:51:43,889 --> 00:51:46,095
Looks like somebody moved it
after the accident.

822
00:51:46,143 --> 00:51:47,987
That would take
half a dozen tow trucks.

823
00:51:48,053 --> 00:51:49,125
Yeah.

824
00:51:49,156 --> 00:51:51,561
And why the hell would
anybody wanna do that?

825
00:51:51,807 --> 00:51:53,135
And the driver?

826
00:51:53,193 --> 00:51:54,325
Not here.

827
00:51:54,864 --> 00:51:58,028
I figure he must have been thrown clear
and wandered off in a daze.

828
00:51:58,151 --> 00:52:00,426
Unless somebody carted him off.

829
00:52:01,773 --> 00:52:03,368
Where did you find this?

830
00:52:03,487 --> 00:52:05,669
Right over there by the shoulder.

831
00:52:07,791 --> 00:52:09,624
Show me exactly.

832
00:52:13,029 --> 00:52:15,055
Heads up.
Here comes trouble.

833
00:52:19,293 --> 00:52:21,353
Yeah, you got that right.

834
00:52:23,702 --> 00:52:26,376
Sheriff, this is getting
way out of hand.

835
00:52:26,455 --> 00:52:28,316
You haul that chief in
for questioning,

836
00:52:28,341 --> 00:52:30,324
and I guarantee you,
he's gonna crack.

837
00:52:30,361 --> 00:52:32,159
Mr. Krantz, there's still no proof...

838
00:52:32,183 --> 00:52:34,000
that the Katonas are
responsible for this.

839
00:52:34,025 --> 00:52:36,915
When are you gonna to wake up
and smell the war paint?

840
00:52:37,329 --> 00:52:39,293
First, three men are missing.

841
00:52:39,634 --> 00:52:40,959
This driver's the fourth.

842
00:52:40,984 --> 00:52:43,103
Say nothing about my property.

843
00:52:43,141 --> 00:52:44,747
Now, it's obvious to me...

844
00:52:44,772 --> 00:52:46,795
that they are responsible,
and I want to know...

845
00:52:46,820 --> 00:52:49,276
when you're going to make an arrest.

846
00:52:49,943 --> 00:52:52,126
Let me ask you a question
for a change.

847
00:52:52,723 --> 00:52:53,834
What?

848
00:52:53,882 --> 00:52:58,021
Have you uncovered anything unusual
recently out at your site?

849
00:52:58,506 --> 00:53:01,475
Now, what's that got to do
with the price of eggs?

850
00:53:01,633 --> 00:53:03,343
Well, have you?

851
00:53:03,458 --> 00:53:05,241
No, I have not.

852
00:53:07,191 --> 00:53:08,642
Well, you realize,
of course, that...

853
00:53:08,667 --> 00:53:12,031
failing to notify the authorities
of a historical find...

854
00:53:12,056 --> 00:53:15,520
on state-granted land
would constitute fraud.

855
00:53:15,854 --> 00:53:18,809
Could even subject the owner
to severe civil and...

856
00:53:18,920 --> 00:53:20,126
criminal penalties.

857
00:53:20,159 --> 00:53:21,445
You know, Sheriff,

858
00:53:21,501 --> 00:53:23,693
I've been in business a long time.

859
00:53:23,759 --> 00:53:27,549
I've gone head to head with
the top men in almost every field.

860
00:53:28,089 --> 00:53:30,264
And I don't intend
to be intimidated...

861
00:53:30,373 --> 00:53:34,770
by some bumpkin lawman
who has a soft spot for his people.

862
00:53:35,706 --> 00:53:38,003
Now, I suggest that
you find out what's going on,

863
00:53:38,028 --> 00:53:39,103
and I mean fast,

864
00:53:39,138 --> 00:53:40,835
because the next phone call I make...

865
00:53:40,860 --> 00:53:43,758
is to your boss in the county office.

866
00:53:44,861 --> 00:53:46,230
Fine.

867
00:53:47,413 --> 00:53:48,714
Here.

868
00:53:51,507 --> 00:53:53,340
Number's on the card.

869
00:53:53,753 --> 00:53:56,303
Excuse me, Mr. Krantz.
Mr. Pomeroy's on the car phone.

870
00:53:56,336 --> 00:53:57,395
He says it's urgent.

871
00:53:57,420 --> 00:53:59,300
- What does he want?
- Uh, he wouldn't say, sir.

872
00:53:59,325 --> 00:54:00,904
All right, we're leaving here anyway.
Come on.

873
00:54:00,929 --> 00:54:02,651
- Yes, sir.
- Let's go.

874
00:54:05,391 --> 00:54:07,606
You complain about
having to get me coffee.

875
00:54:07,639 --> 00:54:09,534
Never again, Sheriff.

876
00:54:12,499 --> 00:54:14,201
What a pair!

877
00:54:15,022 --> 00:54:16,110
All right.

878
00:54:16,151 --> 00:54:17,872
Where was that purse exactly?

879
00:54:17,911 --> 00:54:19,420
Right over here.

880
00:54:21,856 --> 00:54:23,691
Found it sitting right here.

881
00:54:24,323 --> 00:54:26,033
Thanks a lot, Hank.

882
00:54:36,023 --> 00:54:38,063
She came from the woods.

883
00:54:38,512 --> 00:54:39,987
She was running.

884
00:54:40,209 --> 00:54:41,440
Hard.

885
00:54:41,541 --> 00:54:43,575
You can tell all that
just by looking at the grass?

886
00:54:43,611 --> 00:54:46,492
Mm-hm. My grandfather
taught me when I was a kid.

887
00:54:46,861 --> 00:54:48,647
Yeah, but how can you tell?

888
00:54:49,044 --> 00:54:52,380
A good Indian tracker can read
a trail across solid rock.

889
00:54:54,168 --> 00:54:55,699
Come on.

890
00:55:06,780 --> 00:55:08,655
Got something, Sheriff?

891
00:55:08,963 --> 00:55:10,364
Yeah.

892
00:55:11,245 --> 00:55:12,692
Yeah, look here.

893
00:55:12,802 --> 00:55:15,641
This branch was broken
fairly recently.

894
00:55:16,442 --> 00:55:20,365
And it came from, at least,
15 or 20 feet up in these trees.

895
00:55:21,598 --> 00:55:23,794
So, whatever was chasing her...

896
00:55:23,913 --> 00:55:25,519
was at least that tall.

897
00:55:25,564 --> 00:55:27,241
Maybe, a bear?

898
00:55:27,996 --> 00:55:30,141
15-foot bear?
Not likely.

899
00:55:30,189 --> 00:55:31,705
What then?

900
00:55:37,419 --> 00:55:39,149
What's this?

901
00:55:42,797 --> 00:55:44,092
Yeah.

902
00:55:44,163 --> 00:55:46,865
'Cause these relics,
this could be an old Indian's grave.

903
00:55:46,890 --> 00:55:49,497
I thought the ancient tribes
never buried their own in the ground.

904
00:55:49,522 --> 00:55:52,512
No, they burned the bodies
as offerings to their gods.

905
00:55:52,989 --> 00:55:55,299
Monroe to Sheriff Evans,
come in.

906
00:55:58,041 --> 00:56:00,036
This is Evans. Go ahead.

907
00:56:00,139 --> 00:56:01,249
Hey, Steve, uh,

908
00:56:01,274 --> 00:56:03,955
those helicopters haven't found
any sign of that missing driver yet,

909
00:56:03,980 --> 00:56:07,104
but we did spot an abandoned vehicle
along the road to the lake.

910
00:56:07,391 --> 00:56:09,524
All right, we're close.
We'll check it out.

911
00:56:09,656 --> 00:56:12,282
You got it. A couple of patrol cars are
coming down the service road as well.

912
00:56:12,315 --> 00:56:13,704
We'll meet them.

913
00:56:13,729 --> 00:56:15,370
Out. Let's go.

914
00:56:22,360 --> 00:56:23,376
Look, Miss Hayes,

915
00:56:23,401 --> 00:56:27,438
I'm dumping $110 million
into one of your communities.

916
00:56:27,463 --> 00:56:30,815
The least I can get
is a little damn cooperation.

917
00:56:30,886 --> 00:56:32,949
I have to let him run
his investigation.

918
00:56:32,974 --> 00:56:34,261
Investigation?

919
00:56:34,325 --> 00:56:35,722
Is that what you call it?

920
00:56:35,777 --> 00:56:37,787
Because I'm up to my ears in OT pay.

921
00:56:37,812 --> 00:56:39,622
I've got delays upon delays...

922
00:56:39,647 --> 00:56:41,767
because my men won't come to work.

923
00:56:41,792 --> 00:56:44,285
Now, I don't care who's
running this investigation.

924
00:56:44,310 --> 00:56:46,818
I just don't want them
running my corporation...

925
00:56:46,843 --> 00:56:48,624
into the ground while they do it.

926
00:56:48,656 --> 00:56:50,014
I understand.

927
00:56:50,156 --> 00:56:52,809
And I am more than
sympathetic to your position.

928
00:56:52,834 --> 00:56:55,338
However, I can't,
and I will not railroad...

929
00:56:55,363 --> 00:56:58,011
any officers under my jurisdiction...

930
00:56:58,036 --> 00:57:00,528
to bend the law to suit
your financial needs.

931
00:57:00,560 --> 00:57:01,985
Miss Hayes,

932
00:57:02,021 --> 00:57:05,465
if I'm not mistaken,
your term is up in three months.

933
00:57:05,632 --> 00:57:07,513
And you're seeking re-election.

934
00:57:07,615 --> 00:57:09,573
I know this because
a number of people...

935
00:57:09,598 --> 00:57:11,419
in your party have contacted me...

936
00:57:11,459 --> 00:57:13,874
regarding substantial contributions.

937
00:57:13,906 --> 00:57:16,335
Maybe, they think what
I'm doing in your town...

938
00:57:16,360 --> 00:57:18,500
is worth a little more consideration...

939
00:57:18,525 --> 00:57:20,708
than I'm currently being given.

940
00:57:20,840 --> 00:57:22,774
Is that a threat, Mr. Krantz?

941
00:57:22,799 --> 00:57:25,708
Politics and favors
make wonderful bedfellows.

942
00:57:25,733 --> 00:57:27,921
Do you understand
what I am talking about?

943
00:57:27,946 --> 00:57:29,441
Well, I understand this.

944
00:57:29,472 --> 00:57:32,397
I will talk to Sheriff Evans myself.

945
00:57:32,505 --> 00:57:33,846
You just better pray that...

946
00:57:33,870 --> 00:57:36,345
everything going on
at that worksite...

947
00:57:36,370 --> 00:57:38,161
is on the up and up.

948
00:57:38,186 --> 00:57:41,157
Do you understand
what I am talking about?

949
00:57:43,454 --> 00:57:45,594
Good day, Mr. Krantz.

950
00:57:49,384 --> 00:57:52,121
Mr. Krantz, we're here, sir.

951
00:58:04,041 --> 00:58:05,142
Where is it?

952
00:58:05,182 --> 00:58:06,438
This way, sir.

953
00:58:06,467 --> 00:58:08,430
- Jimmy, you wait here.
- Yes, sir.

954
00:58:22,998 --> 00:58:24,927
Anybody else see this?

955
00:58:25,562 --> 00:58:27,895
No, I just uncovered it myself.

956
00:58:28,264 --> 00:58:30,326
I called you as soon as I did.

957
00:58:30,429 --> 00:58:33,517
And I sent the other guys to
the main site as soon as I saw it.

958
00:58:33,542 --> 00:58:36,092
How long do you estimate
it's been here?

959
00:58:37,125 --> 00:58:39,493
Hundred years, maybe two.

960
00:58:40,189 --> 00:58:41,521
Well, I don't care how you do it,

961
00:58:41,546 --> 00:58:42,842
but I want it gone.

962
00:58:42,874 --> 00:58:44,610
You understand?

963
00:58:45,106 --> 00:58:48,104
Mr. Krantz, this is more than
just plowing under some artifacts.

964
00:58:48,129 --> 00:58:49,537
Pomeroy,

965
00:58:50,315 --> 00:58:51,862
do you like your job?

966
00:58:51,905 --> 00:58:53,059
Sir?

967
00:58:53,765 --> 00:58:54,987
You do as I tell you...

968
00:58:55,012 --> 00:58:58,059
and there's a nice bonus
in your next pay envelope.

969
00:58:58,178 --> 00:58:59,765
Okay?

970
00:59:01,215 --> 00:59:03,547
- Mr. Krantz.
- No buts.

971
00:59:03,786 --> 00:59:06,304
You bag up the bones,
and get 'em off my property.

972
00:59:06,329 --> 00:59:08,035
You got it?

973
00:59:09,764 --> 00:59:11,940
Got it, Mr. Krantz.

974
00:59:13,402 --> 00:59:15,086
Good.

975
00:59:16,560 --> 00:59:18,322
Jimmy.

976
00:59:19,424 --> 00:59:21,762
- We're out of here.
- Yes, sir.

977
00:59:26,452 --> 00:59:28,761
Copy. They're running
the plates right now, Sheriff,

978
00:59:28,786 --> 00:59:30,395
but this is Pomeroy's truck all right.

979
00:59:30,420 --> 00:59:32,665
Yeah, I tried to call his father,

980
00:59:32,690 --> 00:59:34,860
but the cell service
is dead out here.

981
00:59:34,936 --> 00:59:36,293
Yeah.

982
00:59:36,324 --> 00:59:38,523
9mm, missing the clip.

983
00:59:38,594 --> 00:59:41,079
- Looks like more of the same, huh?
- Sure does.

984
00:59:41,190 --> 00:59:42,717
What now, boss?

985
00:59:42,755 --> 00:59:45,005
I say, we hitch a ride
back to our cars.

986
00:59:45,030 --> 00:59:46,404
I'll check in at the office.

987
00:59:46,429 --> 00:59:48,047
You stop by the Pomeroy place.

988
00:59:48,072 --> 00:59:49,378
It's on the way.

989
00:59:49,403 --> 00:59:50,984
Roger that.

990
01:00:22,540 --> 01:00:23,725
Where's Storm Cloud?

991
01:00:23,750 --> 01:00:25,003
He is not to be disturbed.

992
01:00:25,035 --> 01:00:26,598
- I will see him now.
- No!

993
01:00:26,629 --> 01:00:29,605
He's on vision quest
seeking a way to undo the evil.

994
01:00:29,636 --> 01:00:32,422
He can't do that!
That fool!

995
01:00:34,360 --> 01:00:37,906
How dare you transgress
the prayers of a chief?

996
01:00:38,652 --> 01:00:40,310
Have you forgotten your place?

997
01:00:40,335 --> 01:00:42,345
I have no place...

998
01:00:42,647 --> 01:00:44,519
with cowards.

999
01:01:20,353 --> 01:01:21,785
Damn!

1000
01:01:54,536 --> 01:01:56,308
Hey, Mark. What's up?

1001
01:01:56,554 --> 01:01:58,103
I wasn't speeding,
not down that hill.

1002
01:01:58,135 --> 01:01:59,579
No, Seth. No tickets today.

1003
01:01:59,603 --> 01:02:01,072
Sheriff wanted me to talk to you.

1004
01:02:01,097 --> 01:02:02,328
Why, what's wrong?

1005
01:02:02,366 --> 01:02:04,426
I'm wondering if you know
where Dex is right now.

1006
01:02:04,577 --> 01:02:05,691
No, what happened?

1007
01:02:05,730 --> 01:02:08,274
I found his truck down by Pine Lake
this morning, abandoned,

1008
01:02:08,298 --> 01:02:09,306
no sign of him.

1009
01:02:09,337 --> 01:02:11,439
So what are we, what are we
talking about, another kidnapping?

1010
01:02:11,464 --> 01:02:13,361
Come on. Can't be sure of that.

1011
01:02:14,060 --> 01:02:15,711
I'm going right down there.

1012
01:02:15,751 --> 01:02:16,909
Where exactly is it?

1013
01:02:16,934 --> 01:02:19,109
You know, I-I'd appreciate it
if you talked to Sheriff first.

1014
01:02:19,134 --> 01:02:20,601
Mark, come on, please.

1015
01:02:20,650 --> 01:02:22,764
Take me to where the truck is.

1016
01:02:22,871 --> 01:02:24,700
What was that?

1017
01:02:29,508 --> 01:02:32,240
Uh, uh, nothing.
I didn't hear anything.

1018
01:02:33,611 --> 01:02:35,534
There it is again.

1019
01:02:39,273 --> 01:02:41,385
What you got in the bag, Seth?

1020
01:02:41,569 --> 01:02:43,321
I, um...

1021
01:02:44,339 --> 01:02:45,825
Seth.

1022
01:02:46,364 --> 01:02:48,134
What's in the bag?

1023
01:03:00,058 --> 01:03:02,378
Mark, get in the truck!

1024
01:03:23,713 --> 01:03:25,569
What the hell is that thing?

1025
01:03:25,694 --> 01:03:26,850
I don't know.

1026
01:03:26,875 --> 01:03:30,299
But it looks like it's gonna
take more than bullets to kill it.

1027
01:04:31,243 --> 01:04:32,769
Oh, my God!

1028
01:04:34,531 --> 01:04:36,166
No!

1029
01:04:42,521 --> 01:04:44,523
- Hey, Steve.
- Jim.

1030
01:04:44,590 --> 01:04:46,460
Any word on Lolli yet?

1031
01:04:46,516 --> 01:04:48,337
No, nothing yet.

1032
01:04:48,384 --> 01:04:50,447
I checked with her mother
and some of her friends...

1033
01:04:50,472 --> 01:04:52,464
and nobody's seen her
since yesterday.

1034
01:04:52,489 --> 01:04:53,783
Mm.

1035
01:04:53,970 --> 01:04:55,566
How about Roberts?
He checked in yet?

1036
01:04:55,595 --> 01:04:56,941
No, not a peep.

1037
01:04:56,996 --> 01:04:58,682
I'll, uh, I'll try to raise him.

1038
01:04:58,707 --> 01:05:00,512
Yeah, he's probably sleeping.

1039
01:05:00,544 --> 01:05:02,099
I could use some myself.

1040
01:05:02,128 --> 01:05:04,448
Oh, uh, Commissioner Hayes called.

1041
01:05:04,473 --> 01:05:06,745
She said, she wants
to talk to you right away.

1042
01:05:06,880 --> 01:05:08,518
Oh, brother!

1043
01:05:08,828 --> 01:05:10,177
How'd she sound?

1044
01:05:10,217 --> 01:05:11,480
Same as usual.

1045
01:05:11,521 --> 01:05:13,116
- Pissed.
- Yeah.

1046
01:05:13,166 --> 01:05:15,761
Get her on the line for me, will you?

1047
01:05:17,003 --> 01:05:18,737
Yeah, sure.

1048
01:05:22,900 --> 01:05:24,003
This is Evans.

1049
01:05:24,028 --> 01:05:25,352
Steve, Hayes.

1050
01:05:25,400 --> 01:05:28,157
What the hell is going on down there?

1051
01:05:28,324 --> 01:05:30,080
What do you mean?

1052
01:05:31,536 --> 01:05:34,789
I've got Richard Krantz
making a lot of noises up here...

1053
01:05:34,814 --> 01:05:36,611
about some Indian uprising...

1054
01:05:36,643 --> 01:05:38,586
against his new development project.

1055
01:05:38,611 --> 01:05:40,828
That's not even close to the truth.

1056
01:05:40,860 --> 01:05:42,813
He says the evidence is overwhelming,

1057
01:05:42,838 --> 01:05:45,166
and you've refused
to make any arrests.

1058
01:05:45,206 --> 01:05:46,330
Hell.

1059
01:05:46,355 --> 01:05:48,880
I could go down there right now
and arrest the whole damn tribe,

1060
01:05:48,905 --> 01:05:51,313
but that's not gonna stop
what's going on.

1061
01:05:51,338 --> 01:05:53,215
Well, it better stop soon.

1062
01:05:53,360 --> 01:05:55,883
There's a bank full of money
at stake here,

1063
01:05:55,915 --> 01:05:57,790
not to mention the political fallout...

1064
01:05:57,815 --> 01:06:00,760
if this project isn't
completed on schedule.

1065
01:06:00,895 --> 01:06:02,152
And if you can't handle it,

1066
01:06:02,177 --> 01:06:04,556
the governor is gonna have
to send in the militia...

1067
01:06:04,581 --> 01:06:07,113
to keep the peace
and protect those workers.

1068
01:06:07,153 --> 01:06:08,438
Got it?

1069
01:06:08,502 --> 01:06:09,895
Yeah.

1070
01:06:10,729 --> 01:06:12,259
Yeah, I got it.

1071
01:06:12,305 --> 01:06:13,405
Good.

1072
01:06:13,437 --> 01:06:15,271
Keep me posted.

1073
01:06:25,732 --> 01:06:27,040
Oh, hey, Steve.

1074
01:06:27,065 --> 01:06:29,820
I tried Roberts twice
on his car radio, still no answer.

1075
01:06:29,860 --> 01:06:31,114
Well, try his apartment.

1076
01:06:31,139 --> 01:06:32,470
If you get him, you let me know.

1077
01:06:32,495 --> 01:06:34,344
Yeah, will do.

1078
01:06:37,386 --> 01:06:38,862
Grandfather,
where are you going?

1079
01:06:38,887 --> 01:06:40,180
It's time.

1080
01:06:40,205 --> 01:06:41,529
I've seen the end.

1081
01:06:41,554 --> 01:06:43,220
We must find the bone axe.

1082
01:06:43,245 --> 01:06:45,577
But it took many warriors
to destroy Torak.

1083
01:06:45,602 --> 01:06:48,081
Kaya, please.
There is no other way.

1084
01:06:48,106 --> 01:06:50,927
- The beast must be stopped.
- No, not the Bone Eater.

1085
01:06:50,975 --> 01:06:53,514
There are too few of you to defeat it.

1086
01:06:53,637 --> 01:06:56,438
I cannot undo what has been done.

1087
01:06:56,509 --> 01:06:58,406
But I can put a stop to it.

1088
01:06:58,521 --> 01:06:59,695
Now please, Kaya.

1089
01:06:59,735 --> 01:07:01,103
Stay with the tribe.

1090
01:07:01,128 --> 01:07:03,164
You'll be safe here.

1091
01:07:18,107 --> 01:07:19,548
Dad!

1092
01:07:20,861 --> 01:07:23,540
Dad, did you find out anything?

1093
01:07:23,714 --> 01:07:25,501
No, nothing yet, Kel.

1094
01:07:26,482 --> 01:07:28,720
Who would do such a thing?

1095
01:07:28,750 --> 01:07:30,363
I don't know, honey.

1096
01:07:30,434 --> 01:07:33,796
We can't assume the worst yet.
She is still just a missing person.

1097
01:07:33,883 --> 01:07:37,260
They've had choppers and search parties
scouring that area all day.

1098
01:07:37,294 --> 01:07:39,723
If she's out there, believe me, honey,
they'll find her.

1099
01:07:39,782 --> 01:07:41,557
Are you sure?

1100
01:07:42,183 --> 01:07:44,149
Hey, I promise.

1101
01:07:44,443 --> 01:07:46,062
I'm doing everything possible.

1102
01:07:46,828 --> 01:07:49,712
Burns to Evans.
Burns to Evans, come in.

1103
01:07:50,188 --> 01:07:51,696
What's up, Big Jim?

1104
01:07:51,733 --> 01:07:55,231
I, I just got a call from the emergency
room over at the trauma center.

1105
01:07:55,300 --> 01:07:56,424
They found Mark...

1106
01:07:56,449 --> 01:07:59,106
lying on the side of the road
up near Whitney Portal.

1107
01:07:59,135 --> 01:08:01,439
They're bringing him in right now.

1108
01:08:01,820 --> 01:08:03,165
What's his condition?

1109
01:08:03,190 --> 01:08:05,076
Well, according to
the paramedics on the scene,

1110
01:08:05,101 --> 01:08:06,530
he's in pretty bad shape.

1111
01:08:06,570 --> 01:08:08,738
They want you over there pronto.

1112
01:08:09,560 --> 01:08:10,790
I'm on my way.

1113
01:08:10,825 --> 01:08:12,814
I'm coming with you.

1114
01:08:15,171 --> 01:08:17,363
All right, all right,
jump in.

1115
01:08:30,112 --> 01:08:32,668
Burns to Evans.
Burns to Evans, come in.

1116
01:08:35,065 --> 01:08:36,742
This is Evans, go ahead.

1117
01:08:36,767 --> 01:08:37,781
Hey, Steve, uh,

1118
01:08:37,806 --> 01:08:39,726
there's a woman here
from the reservation.

1119
01:08:39,751 --> 01:08:40,772
She says that, uh,

1120
01:08:40,812 --> 01:08:43,391
it's imperative that
she speak with you immediately.

1121
01:08:43,512 --> 01:08:44,891
What's her name?

1122
01:08:44,939 --> 01:08:46,228
Kaya.

1123
01:08:47,304 --> 01:08:48,593
Big Jim,

1124
01:08:48,673 --> 01:08:50,886
tell her to meet me
at the hospital.

1125
01:08:54,197 --> 01:08:55,942
Any idea what happened?

1126
01:08:56,910 --> 01:08:58,069
Based on his condition,

1127
01:08:58,094 --> 01:09:00,299
I'd say something
outside of the norm.

1128
01:09:00,362 --> 01:09:01,759
How so?

1129
01:09:04,582 --> 01:09:05,970
Follow me.

1130
01:09:17,998 --> 01:09:19,973
Look, honey. Why don't,
why don't you go out...

1131
01:09:19,998 --> 01:09:21,823
and wait in the hall
while I talk to the doc.

1132
01:09:21,863 --> 01:09:23,037
Okay?

1133
01:09:23,166 --> 01:09:24,815
- Okay.
- All right.

1134
01:09:30,591 --> 01:09:32,788
This one's got me stumped.

1135
01:09:34,844 --> 01:09:36,206
The bones in his right arm...

1136
01:09:36,238 --> 01:09:37,984
and his right hand are completely gone,

1137
01:09:38,009 --> 01:09:40,436
resulting in this fleshy mass.

1138
01:09:41,428 --> 01:09:43,504
What could have done
something like this?

1139
01:09:43,587 --> 01:09:45,562
I'm just a country doctor.

1140
01:09:45,895 --> 01:09:47,597
I'm not a specialist.

1141
01:09:47,828 --> 01:09:49,425
Can he talk?

1142
01:09:50,143 --> 01:09:51,198
Well,

1143
01:09:51,236 --> 01:09:52,903
understandably, he's in shock.

1144
01:09:52,928 --> 01:09:54,801
I wouldn't bring him out.

1145
01:09:55,380 --> 01:09:58,309
Well, did he say anything
when they picked him up?

1146
01:09:58,587 --> 01:09:59,880
Yeah.

1147
01:10:00,546 --> 01:10:03,835
The paramedics said that
he was rambling on about, uh,

1148
01:10:03,860 --> 01:10:05,845
being attacked by some...

1149
01:10:06,162 --> 01:10:07,531
giant...

1150
01:10:07,556 --> 01:10:09,793
skeleton-like creature.

1151
01:10:12,608 --> 01:10:13,811
Obviously,

1152
01:10:13,859 --> 01:10:15,795
a delusion from the pain.

1153
01:10:16,978 --> 01:10:18,200
Yeah.

1154
01:10:18,225 --> 01:10:19,946
Yeah, right.

1155
01:10:23,120 --> 01:10:25,581
You take good care of him, Doc.

1156
01:10:26,270 --> 01:10:28,470
What are you gonna do?

1157
01:10:29,999 --> 01:10:31,895
I'm gonna try to find that...

1158
01:10:31,919 --> 01:10:33,403
delusion.

1159
01:10:53,331 --> 01:10:56,855
I want six others to patrol
that south perimeter.

1160
01:10:57,133 --> 01:11:00,153
You hear so much as an owl fart,

1161
01:11:00,204 --> 01:11:03,122
you shoot first
and ask questions later.

1162
01:11:05,989 --> 01:11:07,147
Mr. Krantz,

1163
01:11:07,180 --> 01:11:08,702
we have a problem
at the main gate.

1164
01:11:08,727 --> 01:11:10,759
- What?
- The Katonas.

1165
01:11:10,893 --> 01:11:13,100
Son of a bitch!

1166
01:11:33,040 --> 01:11:35,959
We request peaceful access
to your property.

1167
01:11:36,056 --> 01:11:38,072
You're too late, Chief.

1168
01:11:38,221 --> 01:11:42,186
You Katonas have taken
this situation way out of hand.

1169
01:11:42,239 --> 01:11:45,292
It is you, Mr. Krantz,
that has broken this ground.

1170
01:11:45,332 --> 01:11:49,299
And it is you that have uncovered
these unholy relics of our ancestors.

1171
01:11:49,386 --> 01:11:51,580
I don't know what
you're talking about.

1172
01:11:51,861 --> 01:11:53,077
The bone axe.

1173
01:11:53,102 --> 01:11:55,006
It was here somewhere,
and we must find it.

1174
01:11:55,054 --> 01:11:57,219
You take one step
through that fence,

1175
01:11:57,244 --> 01:11:59,938
the only thing you're
gonna find is hot lead.

1176
01:11:59,983 --> 01:12:02,141
You understand me?

1177
01:12:04,506 --> 01:12:06,185
What the hell is that?

1178
01:12:06,239 --> 01:12:07,896
- Oh, oh.
- Get out, Mr Krantz.

1179
01:12:07,921 --> 01:12:08,945
Come on, get out of here!

1180
01:12:08,970 --> 01:12:09,984
Come on, let's go!

1181
01:12:11,526 --> 01:12:13,891
Go now! Go! Go!

1182
01:12:33,075 --> 01:12:35,308
- Jimmy, come on!
- Oh, God!

1183
01:12:35,333 --> 01:12:36,411
Oh, oh, God!

1184
01:12:36,436 --> 01:12:37,656
Oh, oh!

1185
01:12:37,681 --> 01:12:39,292
No!

1186
01:12:44,517 --> 01:12:46,546
Dad, who would do that to Mark?

1187
01:12:46,571 --> 01:12:47,903
Well, if you believe Storm Cloud,

1188
01:12:47,928 --> 01:12:49,787
there's some sort of weird
creature running around,

1189
01:12:49,811 --> 01:12:51,692
the Indians call the Bone Eater.

1190
01:12:51,717 --> 01:12:53,295
You don't really believe that.

1191
01:12:53,320 --> 01:12:54,797
Well, something's going on.

1192
01:12:54,821 --> 01:12:56,804
And right now,
nothing is making any sense.

1193
01:12:56,829 --> 01:12:58,689
- Steve!
- What are you doing here?

1194
01:12:58,732 --> 01:13:00,026
It's Storm Cloud.

1195
01:13:00,051 --> 01:13:01,613
What is it?

1196
01:13:01,638 --> 01:13:04,801
He took some of the tribe,
and he went down to the worksite.

1197
01:13:05,684 --> 01:13:07,192
Why?

1198
01:13:07,217 --> 01:13:10,486
He's looking for the sacred war axe.

1199
01:13:11,086 --> 01:13:13,416
Yeah, well, all he's
gonna find is trouble.

1200
01:13:13,441 --> 01:13:14,910
You have to stop him.

1201
01:13:14,935 --> 01:13:18,315
Burns to Evans, Burns to Evans.
Come in, please.

1202
01:13:20,069 --> 01:13:21,612
This is Evans.
Go ahead, Jim.

1203
01:13:21,641 --> 01:13:24,592
Uh, Steve, I just got a call
from the Krantz site.

1204
01:13:24,630 --> 01:13:28,330
They say they're surrounded
by Storm Cloud and his people.

1205
01:13:28,668 --> 01:13:30,430
All right, I'm on it.

1206
01:13:30,576 --> 01:13:33,595
Kaya, take Kelly home
for me, will you?

1207
01:13:33,658 --> 01:13:36,847
I just hope I can get there
before it escalates.

1208
01:13:45,895 --> 01:13:47,965
What's the war axe look like?

1209
01:13:48,075 --> 01:13:51,224
It's an ancient Indian weapon
made with sections of buffalo jaw,

1210
01:13:51,267 --> 01:13:52,678
much like a tomahawk.

1211
01:13:52,817 --> 01:13:54,649
I just saw a tomahawk last night...

1212
01:13:54,690 --> 01:13:56,555
in the back of my boyfriend's truck.

1213
01:13:56,617 --> 01:13:58,549
- It was really old.
- Are you sure?

1214
01:13:58,621 --> 01:13:59,887
I'm positive.

1215
01:13:59,958 --> 01:14:02,419
He said, he just found it
lying around the impound lot.

1216
01:14:02,585 --> 01:14:04,927
We gotta call him right away.

1217
01:14:31,791 --> 01:14:33,448
Storm Cloud?

1218
01:14:37,955 --> 01:14:39,460
Storm Cloud.

1219
01:14:39,762 --> 01:14:41,027
Go, Running Wolf.

1220
01:14:41,075 --> 01:14:42,106
Go now!

1221
01:14:42,130 --> 01:14:44,352
I can't hold it for very long.

1222
01:14:44,589 --> 01:14:45,937
Hold what?

1223
01:15:21,549 --> 01:15:23,421
Sheriff, get in!
Get in!

1224
01:15:23,477 --> 01:15:24,874
Go! Go!

1225
01:15:32,043 --> 01:15:33,980
Sheriff, what the hell
was that thing?

1226
01:15:34,224 --> 01:15:36,385
Something I've got to stop
before tomorrow.

1227
01:15:36,409 --> 01:15:37,496
That I can tell you.

1228
01:15:37,521 --> 01:15:39,721
Do you mind telling me
how you plan to do that?

1229
01:15:39,824 --> 01:15:41,804
You just let me figure it out.

1230
01:15:42,941 --> 01:15:44,518
I appreciate the lift, though.

1231
01:15:44,543 --> 01:15:45,617
Yeah, no problem.

1232
01:15:45,649 --> 01:15:47,411
What the hell were you
doing out here anyway?

1233
01:15:47,436 --> 01:15:49,580
Kelly called me
on my cell phone.

1234
01:15:50,865 --> 01:15:53,060
She wanted me to give you this.

1235
01:15:53,237 --> 01:15:55,532
I found it yesterday
in the impound yard.

1236
01:15:55,576 --> 01:15:57,361
Um, she said, uh,

1237
01:15:57,424 --> 01:15:59,998
she said for you to take
Storm Cloud to the reservation,

1238
01:16:00,033 --> 01:16:02,117
said that he would know
what to do with it.

1239
01:16:02,347 --> 01:16:04,277
Yeah, well, uh,

1240
01:16:06,252 --> 01:16:08,243
Storm Cloud didn't make it.

1241
01:16:11,134 --> 01:16:13,382
Sheriff, no offense, but...

1242
01:16:13,866 --> 01:16:16,123
I really think that
you need to call the army...

1243
01:16:16,148 --> 01:16:18,662
- or the FBI--
- They won't believe it.

1244
01:16:19,190 --> 01:16:21,508
I mean, by the time
they decide this thing is real,

1245
01:16:21,533 --> 01:16:22,648
it'll already be too late.

1246
01:16:22,673 --> 01:16:23,911
All right.

1247
01:16:24,134 --> 01:16:26,025
What are you gonna do about it?

1248
01:16:26,073 --> 01:16:28,017
I want you to drop me off
at the reservation.

1249
01:16:28,049 --> 01:16:30,147
Then I want you
to head back to town.

1250
01:16:30,345 --> 01:16:32,584
You get Kelly
and her friend Kaya.

1251
01:16:32,716 --> 01:16:34,010
You wake 'em up if you have to,

1252
01:16:34,035 --> 01:16:36,207
but I want the three of you
as far from Sweetwater...

1253
01:16:36,232 --> 01:16:37,923
as possible by sunrise.

1254
01:16:38,018 --> 01:16:39,498
All right.

1255
01:16:39,580 --> 01:16:41,215
- What about you?
- Don't worry about me.

1256
01:16:41,240 --> 01:16:43,208
- Sheriff, I can't--
- Mike!

1257
01:16:43,648 --> 01:16:46,473
You gotta be miles away from here
before that eclipse tomorrow.

1258
01:16:46,498 --> 01:16:48,164
You got it?

1259
01:16:49,630 --> 01:16:50,884
Yes, sir.

1260
01:16:55,639 --> 01:16:58,098
So, what's the deal
with this weapon?

1261
01:16:58,253 --> 01:17:00,416
It's the key to stopping all the evil.

1262
01:17:00,558 --> 01:17:02,011
How?

1263
01:17:02,508 --> 01:17:05,106
Come, we must go.
I'll tell you on the way.

1264
01:17:13,167 --> 01:17:15,119
Mike, what is going on?
Where's my father?

1265
01:17:15,144 --> 01:17:16,476
Your father's all right. Okay.

1266
01:17:16,501 --> 01:17:18,341
He went up to the reservation
to get something.

1267
01:17:18,366 --> 01:17:20,257
He went with Storm Cloud?

1268
01:17:20,543 --> 01:17:23,003
The sheriff said,
Storm Cloud didn't make it.

1269
01:17:23,417 --> 01:17:26,356
Oh, my God!
Kaya, I'm so sorry.

1270
01:17:26,622 --> 01:17:27,781
Ladies, listen.

1271
01:17:27,806 --> 01:17:28,988
The sun's gonna be up soon,

1272
01:17:29,013 --> 01:17:31,143
and we gotta be out of here
before the eclipse, okay?

1273
01:17:31,168 --> 01:17:32,952
I'm not leaving without my father.

1274
01:17:32,977 --> 01:17:35,205
Kelly, the last thing that
your father said to me was...

1275
01:17:35,230 --> 01:17:36,727
"Get my daughter and
get her out of town...

1276
01:17:36,752 --> 01:17:37,974
and don't let her talk
you out of it."

1277
01:17:37,999 --> 01:17:39,006
- No, but--
- No, no, no.

1278
01:17:39,031 --> 01:17:40,159
There's gonna be no talking.

1279
01:17:40,184 --> 01:17:42,746
Get in the truck right now.
Both of you, come on.

1280
01:18:06,729 --> 01:18:10,638
I see you're finding your Katona roots.

1281
01:18:20,520 --> 01:18:22,225
Put the knife down.

1282
01:18:22,296 --> 01:18:24,106
Put the axe down first.

1283
01:18:24,664 --> 01:18:26,791
I can't do that.

1284
01:18:29,746 --> 01:18:31,309
I said,

1285
01:18:31,492 --> 01:18:33,769
put the knife down...

1286
01:18:33,904 --> 01:18:35,246
now.

1287
01:18:43,222 --> 01:18:45,302
Whatever you say, Sheriff.

1288
01:18:52,998 --> 01:18:54,768
What's the matter?

1289
01:18:54,833 --> 01:18:57,284
You get soft doing
the white man's bidding, huh?

1290
01:19:27,663 --> 01:19:29,464
May your soul...

1291
01:19:29,731 --> 01:19:31,385
find peace.

1292
01:20:09,032 --> 01:20:10,325
Hyah!

1293
01:20:10,420 --> 01:20:11,841
Hyah!

1294
01:20:49,404 --> 01:20:50,963
It's getting darker.

1295
01:20:51,025 --> 01:20:52,401
Yeah.

1296
01:20:53,352 --> 01:20:55,223
It's starting.

1297
01:22:37,322 --> 01:22:38,639
Whoa!

1298
01:22:38,714 --> 01:22:40,394
Hold on, hold on!

1299
01:22:56,590 --> 01:22:58,399
Oh, my God!

1300
01:23:28,784 --> 01:23:30,230
Dad!

1301
01:23:30,793 --> 01:23:32,166
Baby.

1302
01:23:32,828 --> 01:23:34,714
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

1303
01:23:36,348 --> 01:23:37,913
- All right?
- Yeah.

1304
01:23:43,863 --> 01:23:46,527
Welcome back to the tribe,
Running Wolf.

1305
01:23:47,615 --> 01:23:49,132
I never left.

